-- allium: 3
--
-- pellucid: a Pixelfed client whose user interface is PureScript (Halogen)
-- in a Tauri 2 webview and whose network and secret handling is Rust. It
-- speaks the API that pixelfed-rn speaks to stock Pixelfed servers today,
-- so it can be used against pixelfed.social and any other instance before
-- a Pellucid server exists. This file is the contract the client code is
-- held to: where the code and this file disagree, this file records the
-- intended behaviour and section IMPLEMENTATION STATUS says which rules
-- are built.
--
-- RELATION TO OTHER SPECS. pellucid-server.allium specifies the server
-- Pellucid will need and records how much of it is built. It lived in this
-- directory until 2026-11-10 and is now in the .inference directory of the
-- pellucid-server repository, beside the code it governs. Nothing in this
-- file assumes it: every rule here holds against stock Pixelfed. The fleet side of the
-- test instance is one NixOS module (pixelfed-lab.nix) and is described
-- under surface LabInstance.
--
-- THIS FILE IS CHECKED. `allium check .inference/pellucid.allium` (allium
-- 3.6.1) reports no errors and no warnings. One informational note is
-- expected and stays: external entity Instance has no governing spec,
-- which is true, since Pixelfed's own source governs it. The three
-- revisions before this one were written in Allium's vocabulary but were
-- never run through the checker; it reported 301 errors on the third. The
-- fourth revision is a rewrite into the language the checker accepts.
-- Prose that the language has no form for lives in comments, @guidance,
-- @guarantee and @invariant, where the checker leaves it alone.
--
-- REVISIONS. Written 2026-11-09 against the second batch of the port (the
-- rename to Pellucid, login and feeds, post detail, profile). Revised the
-- same day for the third batch: notifications, compose with media upload,
-- deletion of the viewer's own post, PKCE on login. Rewritten 2026-11-10
-- for the fourth batch: the checker, one paging machine for every list,
-- screens that stay mounted, changes that travel between screens, and the
-- screens Explore, hashtag feed, account lists, bookmarks and likes,
-- settings, profile editor, post editor, reports and direct messages.
--
-- FACTS THIS SPEC IS WRITTEN AGAINST. Checked 2026-11-09 and 2026-11-10 in
-- the source of pixelfed/pixelfed (dev at 6e92465, version 0.15.2, and tag
-- v0.12.5 for what older instances do) and pixelfed/pixelfed-rn (main at
-- da4bcf7). Before the first login to a real Pixelfed account, from
-- winsmuth on 2026-11-10, nothing below had been observed on a running
-- server. The two facts observed since are marked OBSERVED, one under
-- Entities and one under Tooling. Everything else is still from the source
-- alone (KnownIssue lab_instance_undeployed).
--
--   Transport and login
--   - config/cors.php sets allowed_origins to [] unless the operator sets
--     PF_CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS. Only /api/v1/apps and /api/v2/instance set
--     Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * by hand. A page in a browser cannot
--     log in to a stock instance; a native HTTP client can.
--   - The query flag _pe=1 (PF_API_ENTITY_KEY) selects StatusService::get,
--     the Pixelfed entity with pf_type, content_text, liked_by,
--     comments_disabled, place and taggedPeople. Without it
--     StatusService::getMastodon strips those keys.
--   - Login is OAuth 2 authorization code through Laravel Passport on
--     league/oauth2-server 9: GET /api/nodeinfo/2.0.json (software.name
--     pixelfed, version at least 0.12.3), POST /api/v1/apps form-encoded,
--     GET /oauth/authorize, POST /oauth/token, GET
--     /api/v1/accounts/verify_credentials?_pe=1. Both OAuth routes are
--     throttled to 10 requests a minute.
--   - PKCE is accepted and, once a challenge is stored with the code,
--     enforced. /api/v1/apps creates confidential clients only, and
--     Passport demands the secret at /oauth/token.
--   - There is no route through which a client can revoke its own token:
--     no RFC 7009 /oauth/revoke, DELETE /oauth/tokens/{id} needs the
--     browser session, and POST
--     /api/v1.1/accounts/apps-and-applications/{id}/revoke answers 422 for
--     the token making the request.
--
--   Pagination: four schemes
--   - Timelines (home, public), notifications, bookmarks, favourites,
--     mutes, blocks, followed_tags and conversations send a Link header in
--     which rel="next" leads further into the list.
--   - accounts/{id}/followers, accounts/{id}/following,
--     statuses/{id}/favourited_by and statuses/{id}/reblogged_by are
--     cursor-paginated and write Laravel's nextPageUrl() under rel="prev"
--     and previousPageUrl() under rel="next", in 0.12.5 and in 0.15.2
--     alike. Further into the list is rel="prev".
--   - favourited_by and reblogged_by send that header only to the author
--     of the post (or an admin); for anyone else a request carrying
--     cursor answers []. Everyone else sees one page, 80 accounts at most.
--   - accounts/{id}/statuses and /api/v1.1/direct/thread send no Link
--     header and page by max_id. The thread answers eight messages a
--     request, newest first.
--   - timelines/tag/{name} changed: 0.12.5 pages by max_id with no Link
--     header; 0.15.2 sends rel="next" with an opaque signed cursor (at
--     most ten hops, one hour to live) and answers [] to a bare max_id.
--   - follow_requests has no pagination: one request, limit at most 100.
--   - The Link URLs are absolute and built from config('app.url').
--
--   Posts
--   - POST /api/v1/statuses honours _pe. status at most max_caption_length
--     (default 500), media_ids at most max_album_length (default 4),
--     visibility in private, unlisted, public, direct, spoiler_text at
--     most 140. With neither media_ids nor in_reply_to_id it answers 403.
--   - favourite and unfavourite honour _pe and return the Pixelfed entity.
--     bookmark, unbookmark, reblog and unreblog ignore it and return the
--     Mastodon entity.
--   - reblog and unreblog look the post up with whereScope('public'): a
--     post that is not public answers 404. The share is counted by a
--     queued job, so reblogs_count in the answer is the count before it.
--   - GET /api/v1/bookmarks honours _pe. GET /api/v1/favourites does not
--     and always returns the Mastodon entity.
--   - PUT /api/v1/statuses/{id} (StatusEditController) accepts status,
--     spoiler_text (140), sensitive, media_ids and location; only the
--     author, only a post that is not a share, at most ten edits. For a
--     post with more than one attachment UpdateStatusService reads
--     media_ids unconditionally and deletes from storage every attachment
--     the list leaves out. The answer is the Pixelfed entity.
--   - DELETE /api/v1/statuses/{id} returns the deleted status.
--   - GET /api/v1/statuses/{id}/context honours _pe, returns up to 100
--     descendants and sends no Link header.
--   - POST /api/v2/media is multipart with file and an optional
--     description; the answer has url null and preview_url set. PUT
--     /api/v1/media/{id} sets the description. GET
--     /api/v1.1/compose/settings returns the instance's limits.
--
--   Accounts
--   - GET /api/v1/accounts/relationships takes id[] and returns id,
--     following, followed_by, blocking, muting, requested and more. The
--     viewer's own id yields no entry.
--   - follow, unfollow, block, unblock, mute and unmute each answer with
--     the relationship. block also deletes the follow in both directions
--     and refuses an admin and the viewer's own account with 400.
--   - follow_requests/{id}/authorize and /reject answer with the
--     relationship.
--   - POST /api/v1/accounts/update_credentials honours _pe and validates
--     display_name at most 30, note at most 200, website at most 120,
--     locked, and avatar as a multipart file.
--   - A locked account the viewer does not follow, and one that hides
--     its followers or following, answer [] to the matching list.
--
--   Search, discover, hashtags
--   - GET /api/v2/search validates q as 1 to 100 characters and returns
--     accounts, hashtags and statuses; SearchApiV2Service::statuses
--     returns [] unconditionally. With _pe a hashtag is name, url,
--     history, count. resolve lets a full handle or URL be looked up on
--     another server.
--   - /api/v1.1/discover/posts/trending?range=daily|monthly|yearly returns
--     up to 30 local public posts ordered by likes;
--     /api/v1.1/discover/accounts/popular up to 16 accounts the viewer
--     does not follow; /api/v1.1/discover/posts/hashtags a list of id,
--     total, name ("#tag"), hashtag ("tag"), url.
--   - GET /api/v1/tags/{name} returns name, url, history, following and,
--     with _pe, count; an unknown tag answers following false rather than
--     404. tags/{name}/follow answers 422 for an unknown tag.
--     FollowedTagResource is [] for a tag the server could not load.
--
--   Reports and direct messages
--   - POST /api/v1.1/report takes report_type in spam, sensitive, abusive,
--     underage, violence, copyright, impersonation, scam, terrorism;
--     object_type in post, user, story, direct_message; object_id; and an
--     optional message of at most 255 bytes after cleaning. A report on
--     the viewer's own content and a second report on the same object
--     answer 400.
--   - GET /api/v1/conversations returns id (a number on 0.12, a string on
--     0.15), unread, accounts and last_status. GET
--     /api/v1.1/direct/thread?pid= returns the other person and messages
--     of id, isAuthor, type, text, media, created_at, timeAgo, seen. POST
--     /api/v1.1/direct/thread/send takes to_id, message and type in text,
--     emoji; the message limit is 500 on 0.12 and 2000 on 0.15, and 0.12
--     omits created_at from the answer. DELETE
--     /api/v1.1/direct/thread/message?id= is for the author only.
--
--   Notifications
--   - GET /api/v1/notifications honours _pe, caps limit at 40 and pages by
--     the Link header. NotificationTransformer maps verbs to follow,
--     mention, share, favourite, comment, tagged, modlog, direct,
--     story:react, story:comment. The status is the liked or shared post
--     for a like or a share, the comment itself for a comment, the
--     mentioning post for a mention, and absent for a follow.
--
--   Entities
--   - A transformer either casts a field or passes the database row's
--     value through. StatusTransformer, AccountTransformer and
--     RelationshipTransformer cast their ids with (string) and their
--     flags with (bool). What they pass through uncast: favourites_count
--     (likes_count), visibility (scope, else visibility; can be null) and
--     content_text (caption; can be null).
--   - MediaTransformer casts id and nothing else. is_nsfw is the media
--     row's column, which the Media model does not cast: 0 or 1 from the
--     database, null on a fresh upload whose model was never read back.
--     meta.original.width and height are the row's values too, numbers or
--     strings depending on the database driver. OBSERVED 2026-11-10: on a
--     real server the first attachment of the first home timeline post
--     carried an is_nsfw that was neither a boolean nor null.
--   - NotificationTransformer's tagged is { username, post_url,
--     status_id, profile_id }, with status_id and profile_id as bare
--     numbers from the media_tags row. A Pixelfed id is larger than
--     2^53 - 1, so JSON.parse has already rounded status_id by the time
--     the client reads it. post_url is the tagged post's url, which for a
--     post made on that server ends in the same id as text.
--   - The home timeline (dev) drops, on the server, a post with no
--     account.id and a share with no inner post before it answers.
--   - Counters have shipped as numbers, as strings and as null.
--   - liked_by is { username: null, others: false } when there is nobody
--     to show.
--   - Status created_at carries three fractional digits, Account
--     created_at six, a direct message's an offset instead of Z. All
--     three start with the same nineteen characters.
--
--   Tooling
--   - Tauri 2: app.withGlobalTauri exposes window.__TAURI__.core.invoke
--     and .event.listen with no npm package; invoke(cmd, Uint8Array,
--     { headers }) sends the bytes as the raw IPC body.
--   - An empty location hash is not the path "/": routing-duplex parses
--     "/" as the home route and fails on "". The address bar holds "" when
--     the app starts and returns to it on history.back().
--   - Window.scrollY, Window.innerHeight, Window.scroll and
--     Element.scrollHeight are in purescript-web-html and
--     purescript-web-dom; no foreign module is needed to read or set the
--     scroll position.
--   - WebKitGTK plays <video> and <audio> through GStreamer and finds
--     plugins at run time on GST_PLUGIN_SYSTEM_PATH_1_0. In the locked
--     nixpkgs (webkitgtk 2.54.2, GStreamer 1.28.8) it is built against
--     gst-plugins-base and gst-plugins-bad and propagates neither, so a
--     shell that lists only webkitgtk puts no plugin on that path. When a
--     media element loads and the webvttenc element (gst-plugins-bad) is
--     not found, WebKit logs one line about a missing WebVTT encoder. A
--     feed video is rendered with preload=metadata, so it loads as soon
--     as it is drawn. OBSERVED 2026-11-10 on winsmuth: sixteen such lines
--     in one run of cargo tauri dev from a shell with no GStreamer
--     package in it.
--
-- DECISIONS. D1 to D22 were taken 2026-11-09; D23 to D32 on 2026-11-10;
-- D33 and D34 on 2026-11-11.
--
--   D1. SCOPE. A client for the existing Pixelfed protocol first. The
--       server is a later project with its own spec.
--   D2. THE SPLIT. Rust (crate pixelfed-core, no UI, no Tauri dependency)
--       owns the OAuth dance, the token, the authenticated transport and
--       the validation of every URL the token travels to. PureScript owns
--       the entities, the decoders, the screens and the state. The Tauri
--       crate is an adapter and holds no protocol logic.
--   D3. THE TOKEN NEVER CROSSES THE BRIDGE. The webview receives
--       SessionSummary and never the access token, the client secret or
--       the refresh token.
--   D4. THE TOKEN GOES ONLY TO /api/ PATHS ON THE LOGGED-IN ORIGIN. A
--       request path must start with /api/. A pagination cursor is used
--       only after Rust parses it and checks scheme, host, port and path.
--   D5. HTTPS ONLY. There is no insecure mode and none is planned. D34
--       makes one exception, for development builds and for the address
--       127.0.0.1 alone.
--   D6. NO HTML IS RENDERED AS HTML. Captions are content_text; where a
--       server omits it the HTML content is reduced to text. innerHTML is
--       not used anywhere.
--   D7. NO NPM. The frontend is spago packages plus two hand-written
--       foreign modules, both listed in contract ForeignBudget.
--   D8. ONLY WHAT IDENTIFIES A THING CAN FAIL ITS DECODE. Every read
--       sends _pe=1. A post needs its id and its account; an account, and
--       a mention, its id and username; an attachment, a notification, a
--       relationship, a message and a thread their id; a conversation
--       its id and its last message; a hashtag its name. Every other
--       field is read by a reader that accepts each encoding the server
--       uses and falls back to a default for anything else: a flag is
--       true or false, 1 or 0, or one of those in a string; a number is a
--       number or a string of digits; a text field that is absent, null
--       or of another type is empty or absent. An id is a string, or a
--       whole number no larger than
--       2^53 - 1; a larger number has lost its last digits in JSON.parse
--       and is refused, because what is left names another post. Unknown
--       visibilities, pf_types, media types and notification verbs are
--       kept as data. One field of an unexpected type never takes a
--       timeline with it (KnownIssue uncast_fields_failed_the_timeline).
--   D9. THE SERVER IS THE TRUTH FOR TOGGLES. A like, bookmark or share
--       shows the old state until the server answers. The favourite
--       endpoints return the Pixelfed entity, which replaces ours; the
--       bookmark and share endpoints return the Mastodon entity, from
--       which only the flag is taken. The share count moves by one
--       locally when the flag flips, because the server's own count is
--       read before its queue has counted the share. A reply or a deleted
--       comment moves the reply count by one locally.
--   D10. ONE LOGIN FLOW, TWO REDIRECTS. The desktop shell binds a one-shot
--        listener on 127.0.0.1; a mobile shell will register a custom
--        scheme and hand the same code to the same login_finish.
--   D11. A FRESH CLIENT PER LOGIN.
--   D12. SESSION STORAGE IS A SEAM. SecretStore is a trait; the desktop
--        implementation is a JSON file with mode 0600.
--   D13. LOGOUT IS LOCAL. The server keeps the token until it expires.
--   D14. PAGINATION FOLLOWS WHAT THE SERVER GIVES. Superseded in mechanism
--        by D23; the rule stands: the client never builds or edits a
--        cursor, and pages by max_id only where the server gives none.
--   D15. THE GATE. scripts/check.fish: purs-tidy check, spago build
--        --strict, spago test, cargo fmt --check, cargo clippy -D warnings
--        and cargo test for the core, the bundle into dist/, cargo clippy
--        -D warnings for the shell. Nothing is delivered with a warning.
--   D16. A THROWAWAY INSTANCE ON BLADE.
--   D17. THE NAME. Pellucid, meaning transparently clear.
--   D18. RELEASE. AGPL-3.0-or-later. Not released until the port covers
--        what people use daily and the mobile shell exists.
--   D19. PKCE ALWAYS, SECRET STILL.
--   D20. MEDIA BYTES CROSS THE BRIDGE AS A RAW IPC BODY, ONCE.
--   D21. COMPOSE REQUIRES MEDIA AND UPLOADS FIRST.
--   D22. DELETING A POST TAKES TWO TAPS AND NO DIALOG. Extended by D29.
--
--   D23. ONE PAGING MACHINE. Every list is a Pager: a function that
--        fetches one chunk and, when the server offers more, the pager
--        for the chunk after it. Pixelfed.Client builds a pager per
--        endpoint from the scheme that endpoint uses; a screen sees none
--        of the four schemes. App.Paged is the one state machine every
--        paginated screen runs, and it is pure. Its rules: no chunk is
--        requested twice, no item appears twice, a chunk with nothing new
--        ends the list even when the server offers another cursor, and an
--        answer nobody is waiting for is dropped.
--   D24. SCREENS STAY MOUNTED. Root keeps a stack of screens. A route
--        change is a step back when it names the route directly
--        underneath, a switch of tab when it names one of the six tab
--        routes, and a step forward otherwise. The screen underneath a
--        step forward stays mounted with its state and its scroll
--        position, so going back fetches nothing and lands where the
--        person left. At most twelve screens are kept; beyond that the
--        oldest above the tab's own screen is dropped.
--   D25. CHANGES TRAVEL BETWEEN SCREENS. A screen that changes a post,
--        deletes one or changes the viewer's own account raises an
--        output; Root turns it into a query for every mounted screen
--        that shows the same thing. This is what D24 costs: a screen
--        underneath is no longer rebuilt from the server on return.
--   D26. THE PAGE SCROLLS THE LIST. Root listens for window scroll events
--        and, when less than 800 CSS pixels of page lie below the
--        viewport, tells the screen in front, and only that one. A list
--        answers by fetching its next chunk. The Load more button stays as
--        the fallback and as the retry after a failure.
--   D27. LINKS COME FROM THE TEXT, NOT FROM THE MARKUP. A caption is
--        split by one pattern into text, #hashtag and @mention runs. A
--        hashtag opens the feed of that name. A mention is a link only
--        when the status lists an account whose acct or username matches,
--        because that is where the account id comes from. The sign must
--        not follow a letter, a digit or one of _ / & # @ ., which keeps
--        e-mail addresses and URL fragments as text.
--   D28. LISTS OF ACCOUNTS, HASHTAGS AND MESSAGES DROP WHAT THEY CANNOT
--        READ. The server itself filters such lists and has shipped false
--        and [] in place of an entry. The lists inside a post
--        (attachments, tags, mentions) do the same. A list of posts and
--        the list of notifications stay strict about what D8 requires: a
--        post that cannot be identified, or a share whose inner post
--        cannot, fails the page with an error that names the index and
--        the field, which the person sees and can retry, so a post never
--        goes missing without a trace. A notification's actor or post
--        that cannot be read is absent from the row instead.
--   D29. WHAT CANNOT BE UNDONE ASKS FIRST, IN THE PAGE. Deleting a post,
--        blocking an account and logging out each take a second tap on a
--        confirmation strip. No window.confirm(): a native dialog blocks
--        the webview's IPC. Deleting a comment or a direct message, and
--        unfollowing, muting and unblocking, act at once.
--   D30. AN EDIT SENDS EVERY ATTACHMENT BACK. The post editor changes
--        caption, sensitivity and content warning only, and always sends
--        the post's full list of media ids in order.
--   D31. THE EMPTY HASH IS HOME. parseRoute reads "" as the home route.
--        Without that, going back to the first screen of a restarted app
--        changed the address and nothing else.
--   D32. LIMITS ARE THE LOWER OF WHAT SERVERS ENFORCE. A direct message is
--        capped at 500 characters, a report note at 255, a display name at
--        30, a bio at 200, a website at 120, a content warning at 140, a
--        search at 100. Each is the server's own validation rule; where
--        versions differ the lower one is used.
--   D33. TWO KINDS OF SERVER. The client signs in to a Pixelfed at
--        min_pixelfed_version or newer and to a pellucid-server at
--        min_pellucid_version or newer, told apart by the name each gives
--        for itself in nodeinfo. Each kind has its own floor: Pixelfed's
--        is not applied to a Pellucid server, whose first release is
--        0.1.0. Any other name is refused. pellucid-server speaks the
--        same client API, and where its answers differ from Pixelfed's
--        they are the stricter form (every id a string, every flag a
--        boolean), which the decoders of D8 already read.
--   D34. A DEVELOPMENT BUILD REACHES A SERVER ON ITS OWN MACHINE OVER
--        PLAIN HTTP. Typed with its scheme and by its address, as in
--        http://127.0.0.1:8080, a server is reached over http by a build
--        with debug assertions (cargo tauri dev, cargo test). A build
--        without them refuses that text where it is typed and where it
--        is read back from a saved session, so a release binary cannot
--        hold such a domain at all. The reason is D5's own: a request to
--        127.0.0.1 does not leave the machine, so there is no network to
--        read the token from. The other way to reach a local server,
--        trusting a private certificate authority, would open more than
--        this does, because the core trusts only the authorities
--        compiled into it and would need a way to be told about others.
--        Nothing is downgraded. http:// in front of any other host is
--        reached over https as before; that covers the name localhost,
--        which is whatever the resolver says it is, and the rest of
--        127.0.0.0/8, which the webview's policy cannot name. 127.0.0.1
--        typed without a scheme is https too. The domain is stored and
--        shown with its scheme, so the settings screen says what the
--        session talks to. What the exception costs: on a machine with
--        other users, whoever binds the port is the server, and receives
--        the password typed into the consent page and the token after
--        it.
--
-- IMPLEMENTATION STATUS at 2026-11-11 (the fourth batch, the decoder
-- revision that followed the first real login, then D33 and D34):
--
--   BUILT      D2 to D9, D11, D13 to D15, D17, D19 to D34. Every rule in
--              this file. Surfaces Platform, InstanceAnswers, Bridge,
--              LoginScreen, SignedInShell, TimelineScreen, TagFeedHeader,
--              ListScreens, PostDetailScreen, FormScreens, ExploreScreen,
--              ProfileScreen, ThreadScreen, NotificationsScreen,
--              ComposeScreen, SettingsScreen, DevShell. The Rust core has
--              30 unit tests, one of them for the Pellucid server's
--              name and floor (D33), six for D34 as both kinds of build
--              apply it, and one for a session file that cannot be read;
--              the PureScript side has 184 checks (decoders against
--              fixtures shaped like the server's transformers, uncast
--              fields included, and against loose payloads; the paging
--              machine, the navigation stack, the route codec, caption
--              links, the merge rules); the bundled UI passes a 122-step
--              headless run against a mock of contract Shell (KnownIssue
--              smoke_harness_external). The shell crate compiles and is
--              clippy-clean.
--   RUN        2026-11-11, against a pellucid-server on the same machine
--              at http://127.0.0.1:8080 (D34), where this spec is
--              written and not on winsmuth. The core alone: probe,
--              sign-in through the server's consent page, 25 uploads and
--              posts, two pages of the home timeline by cursor, four
--              cursors to other origins refused before the network, the
--              session read back from its file. Then the desktop shell
--              itself, the debug binary on a display with no screen
--              (WebKitGTK 2.52.6), driven by synthetic pointer and
--              keyboard: the address typed into the login screen, the
--              consent page answered by a script standing in for the
--              browser, the feeds with their pictures, a profile and its
--              grid, a follow, a post's own screen, the composer's limits
--              as the server states them, and the settings screen naming
--              the session as http://127.0.0.1:8080. A like, Alerts and
--              Explore show the server's 404, which is what a server
--              without those routes should produce. The same binary
--              built without devCsp showed every picture as a blocked
--              box. Not run: choosing a file in the composer (the file
--              dialog did not take a path from a synthetic keyboard), so
--              an upload has gone through the core and not through the
--              webview; and cargo tauri dev, which may serve the page
--              from the command's own web server where the binary run
--              here served it through Tauri's protocol. The core's 30
--              tests also pass compiled as a release build, in which the
--              address of D34 is refused and a saved session carrying it
--              does not read back.
--   PARTIAL    D10: the desktop redirect is built and tested; the deep
--              link branch is not written. D12: FileStore only. D16: the
--              module is written and parses; it has not been deployed.
--   NOT BUILT  D18. Stories, collections, the admin screens, push
--              notifications, avatar upload, a recipient picker for a new
--              conversation, sending media in a direct message, blocked
--              domains, notification type filters, post edit history,
--              cropping and location tagging in the composer, blurhash
--              placeholders, a Nix package for the bundle and the desktop
--              binary, the Android and iOS shells. Token revocation is
--              impossible against stock Pixelfed.

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Given
------------------------------------------------------------

given {
    app: App
    core: Core
    login: LoginForm
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- External Entities
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A Pixelfed server as the client meets it: one https origin, the
-- Mastodon-shaped API with Pixelfed's additions, OAuth 2 through Laravel
-- Passport. Governed by Pixelfed's own source, not by a spec.
external entity Instance {
    domain: Domain
    software: String
    version: String
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Value Types
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Opaque JSON and opaque bytes.
value Json {}

value Bytes {}

-- A validated host. parse accepts an optional scheme, trailing slashes
-- and mixed case, rejects paths, queries, userinfo and hosts without a
-- dot (localhost excepted), lower-cases, and keeps an explicit port. The
-- base URL is https (D5) unless plain_http is set, which only D34 sets:
-- then the base URL is http and the stored text carries the scheme.
value Domain {
    host: String
    port: Integer?
    plain_http: Boolean
}

-- An absolute URL taken from a Link header. The UI holds it as a string
-- it may not dereference; only Shell.api_follow may, after validation.
value Cursor {
    url: String
}

value ApiRequest {
    method: Method
    path: String
    query: List<String>
    body: Json?
}

value ApiResponse {
    status: Integer
    body: Json
    next: Cursor?
    prev: Cursor?
}

-- What the UI may know about who is logged in.
value SessionSummary {
    domain: String
    account_id: String?
    acct: String?
}

-- Serialised as { kind, message, status? } so the UI decodes a closed sum.
value AppError {
    kind: ErrorKind
    message: String
    status: Integer?
}

value InstanceProbe {
    domain: String
    software: String
    version: String
}

-- One file for POST /api/v2/media. The bytes are the raw IPC body (D20).
value MediaUpload {
    bytes: Bytes
    filename: String
    mime: String
    description: String?
}

-- RFC 7636. The verifier never leaves Rust.
value Pkce {
    verifier: String
    challenge: String
}

-- Where the app is. The three optional parts carry the route's argument;
-- which one is present follows from kind.
value Route {
    kind: RouteKind
    account_id: String?
    status_id: String?
    tag: String?
}

value Account {
    id: String
    username: String
    acct: String
    display_name: String
    note: String
    note_text: String?
    url: String
    avatar: String
    locked: Boolean
    followers_count: Integer
    following_count: Integer
    statuses_count: Integer
    website: String?
}

value MediaAttachment {
    id: String
    media_type: MediaType
    url: String
    preview_url: String?
    description: String?
}

value Mention {
    id: String
    username: String
    acct: String
}

-- A post as the client holds it. content is HTML and is never rendered as
-- such (D6); reblog_of is the id of the post a share wraps.
value Status {
    id: String
    account: Account
    created_at: String
    edited_at: String?
    content: String
    content_text: String?
    visibility: Visibility
    sensitive: Boolean
    spoiler_text: String
    pf_type: PfType
    media: List<MediaAttachment>
    mentions: List<Mention>
    favourites_count: Integer
    reblogs_count: Integer
    reply_count: Integer
    favourited: Boolean
    reblogged: Boolean
    bookmarked: Boolean
    comments_disabled: Boolean
    in_reply_to_id: String?
    reblog_of: String?
}

value Relationship {
    id: String
    following: Boolean
    followed_by: Boolean
    blocking: Boolean
    muting: Boolean
    requested: Boolean
}

value Hashtag {
    name: String
    following: Boolean
    count: Integer?
}

value Notification {
    id: String
    kind: NotificationKind
    created_at: String
    actor_id: String?
    status_id: String?
    in_reply_to_id: String?
    -- The last segment of tagged.post_url when that is a number, else
    -- tagged.status_id when it arrived exact, else absent (D8).
    tagged_status_id: String?
}

value Message {
    id: String
    is_author: Boolean
    kind: String
    text: String
    media: String?
    created_at: String
    time_ago: String
    seen: Boolean
}

value Conversation {
    id: String
    unread: Boolean
    other_account_id: String?
    last_id: String
    last_text: String
    last_at: String
}

-- GET /api/v1.1/compose/settings. Sizes are kilobytes.
value ComposeSettings {
    allowed_media_types: List<String>
    max_caption_length: Integer
    max_file_size_kb: Integer
    max_media_attachments: Integer
    max_alt_text_length: Integer
    default_visibility: Visibility?
}

-- One run of a caption (D27).
value Segment {
    kind: SegmentKind
    text: String
    account_id: String?
}

-- One chunk of a list and whether the server offers more behind it.
value Chunk {
    keys: List<String>
    has_next: Boolean
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Contracts
------------------------------------------------------------

-- crates/pixelfed-core. No UI, no webview, no Tauri. Everything that
-- touches the network or the token.
contract CoreApi {
    probe: (domain: Domain) -> InstanceProbe
    login_begin: (domain: Domain) -> PendingLogin
    login_finish: (pending: PendingLogin) -> SessionSummary
    logout: () -> Boolean
    api_request: (request: ApiRequest) -> ApiResponse
    api_follow: (url: String) -> ApiResponse
    media_upload: (upload: MediaUpload) -> ApiResponse
    session_summary: () -> SessionSummary

    @invariant ServerNameIsTheServers
        -- probe accepts a server whose nodeinfo software.name is
        -- pixelfed or pellucid, compared without case, and whose version
        -- is at least that kind's floor (D33). The name compared is the
        -- one the server gives for itself. The server software pellucid
        -- and this app share a name; a server is accepted for running
        -- that software at a supported version, and for no other reason
        -- (instance::check_software, SUPPORTED_SERVERS).

    @invariant ApiPathsOnly
        -- api_request refuses a path not starting with /api/ before any
        -- network activity (api::request_url).

    @invariant UploadsBounded
        -- media_upload refuses an empty body and a body over
        -- max_upload_bytes before any network activity (api::upload).

    @invariant PkceAlways
        -- login_begin generates a fresh Pkce; the authorize URL carries
        -- code_challenge and code_challenge_method=S256; the token request
        -- sends code_verifier (tested against RFC 7636 appendix B).

    @invariant CursorsValidated
        -- api_follow parses the URL and requires the session domain's
        -- scheme, host and port, and a path under /api/. The scheme is
        -- https for every domain but the one D34 allows, and for that
        -- one an https cursor is refused like any other foreign origin.

    @invariant UnreadableSessionIsNoSession
        -- Core::new takes a session the store cannot read as no session
        -- and leaves the file where it is; the next sign-in replaces it
        -- and a logout removes it. A release build meets this when the
        -- file was written by a development build signed in under D34.
        -- Before 2026-11-11 Core::new failed instead, the shell's setup
        -- failed with it, and the process ended before a window existed.

    @invariant RedirectsDropTheToken
        -- reqwest follows at most five redirects and removes
        -- Authorization when the host changes.

    @invariant ErrorsAreTyped
        -- Every failure is an AppError. A non-2xx answer becomes http with
        -- the server's error or message field, or the first 200
        -- characters of the body.

    @guidance
        -- Modules: domain, instance, oauth, link, api, session, store,
        -- core. User agent Pellucid/<version> (+https://harryprayiv.com).
        -- Request timeout 30 s, which bounds an upload too; login timeout
        -- 10 min. Every operation that can fail returns AppError in place
        -- of the type shown.
}

-- Where the session is persisted.
contract SecretStore {
    load: () -> Session
    save: (session: Session) -> Boolean
    clear: () -> Boolean

    @invariant DesktopFileIsPrivate
        -- FileStore writes <app data dir>/session.json through a temporary
        -- file with mode 0600 and renames it into place; load tolerates a
        -- missing file and reports a corrupt one as storage.

    @guidance
        -- Mobile stores are not written. The trait is the only thing a
        -- platform store has to implement.
}

-- src-tauri. The IPC the webview sees: seven commands and two events,
-- session-changed (a SessionSummary or null) and login-failed (an
-- AppError).
contract Shell {
    session_get: () -> SessionSummary
    instance_probe: (domain: String) -> InstanceProbe
    login_start: (domain: String) -> String
    logout: () -> Boolean
    api_request: (request: ApiRequest) -> ApiResponse
    api_follow: (url: String) -> ApiResponse
    media_upload: (body: Bytes, filename: String, mime: String, description: String) -> ApiResponse

    @invariant NoProtocolLogic
        -- Each command calls one CoreApi operation; the only extra
        -- behaviour is opening the system browser, emitting the two
        -- events, and unpacking the raw body and percent-decoding the
        -- three headers of media_upload.

    @invariant TokenAbsent
        -- No command result and no event payload contains access_token,
        -- client_secret or refresh_token (D3).

    @guidance
        -- tauri.conf.json: withGlobalTauri true; CSP default-src 'self';
        -- script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' https: data:
        -- blob:; media-src https: blob:; connect-src ipc:
        -- http://ipc.localhost; font-src 'self'; object-src 'none';
        -- base-uri 'none'. devCsp is the same policy with
        -- http://127.0.0.1:* added to img-src and media-src (D34). Tauri
        -- applies devCsp in a build without its custom-protocol feature,
        -- which is what cargo tauri dev and a plain cargo build produce,
        -- and csp in what cargo tauri build produces. cargo tauri build
        -- --debug therefore accepts the address of D34 and shows no
        -- picture from it. Capability default: core:default only.
        -- Nothing in the fourth batch added a command: every new screen
        -- goes through api_request and api_follow.
}

-- src/App/Backend.purs: the record every screen uses, one field per Shell
-- command plus the two subscriptions. App.Backend.Tauri implements it.
contract Backend {
    session_get: () -> SessionSummary
    instance_probe: (domain: String) -> InstanceProbe
    login_start: (domain: String) -> String
    logout: () -> Boolean
    api_request: (request: ApiRequest) -> ApiResponse
    api_follow: (cursor: Cursor) -> ApiResponse
    media_upload: (upload: MediaUpload) -> ApiResponse

    @invariant NeverThrows
        -- Both foreign invokes resolve to { ok, value } or { ok, error }
        -- and never reject; a thrown exception, an IPC rejection, an
        -- AppError and an undecodable payload all become Left AppError.

    @guidance
        -- A second implementation over fetch would serve a Pellucid server
        -- that sets CORS headers. It is not written.
}

-- D7. Every foreign function in the frontend. A foreign module not
-- listed here is not in the tree; test fixtures are read by
-- test/Test/Main.js, which is test code and not shipped.
contract ForeignBudget {
    invoke_impl: (command: String, payload: Json) -> Json
    invoke_raw_impl: (command: String, body: Bytes, headers: Json) -> Json
    listen_impl: (event: String) -> Boolean
    array_buffer_impl: (file: Bytes) -> Bytes

    @invariant Named
        -- App.Backend.Tauri.js supplies the first three over
        -- window.__TAURI__; Util.File.js supplies the fourth,
        -- file.arrayBuffer(). The fourth batch added none: scrolling,
        -- history and the caption pattern use spago packages only.
}

-- Pixelfed.Client: one pager per list endpoint (D23). Each names the
-- route and the scheme it pages by.
contract Pagers {
    home: () -> Chunk                                   -- GET /api/v1/timelines/home?_pe=1&limit=20          Link next
    public: () -> Chunk                                 -- GET /api/v1/timelines/public?_pe=1&limit=20        Link next
    bookmarks: () -> Chunk                              -- GET /api/v1/bookmarks?_pe=1&limit=20               Link next
    favourites: () -> Chunk                             -- GET /api/v1/favourites?limit=20                    Link next, Mastodon entity
    tag: (name: String) -> Chunk                        -- GET /api/v1/timelines/tag/{name}?_pe=1&limit=20    Link next, else max_id
    account_statuses: (account_id: String) -> Chunk     -- GET /api/v1/accounts/{id}/statuses?_pe=1&limit=24  max_id
    notifications: () -> Chunk                          -- GET /api/v1/notifications?_pe=1&limit=20           Link next
    followers: (account_id: String) -> Chunk            -- GET /api/v1/accounts/{id}/followers?_pe=1&limit=20 Link prev
    following: (account_id: String) -> Chunk            -- GET /api/v1/accounts/{id}/following?_pe=1&limit=20 Link prev
    liked_by: (status_id: String) -> Chunk              -- GET /api/v1/statuses/{id}/favourited_by?_pe=1      Link prev, author only
    shared_by: (status_id: String) -> Chunk             -- GET /api/v1/statuses/{id}/reblogged_by?_pe=1       Link prev, author only
    mutes: () -> Chunk                                  -- GET /api/v1/mutes?limit=40                         Link next
    blocks: () -> Chunk                                 -- GET /api/v1/blocks?limit=40                        Link next
    follow_requests: () -> Chunk                        -- GET /api/v1/follow_requests?limit=40               one request
    followed_tags: () -> Chunk                          -- GET /api/v1/followed_tags?limit=100                Link next
    conversations: () -> Chunk                          -- GET /api/v1/conversations?limit=20                 Link next
    thread: (account_id: String) -> Chunk               -- GET /api/v1.1/direct/thread?pid={id}               max_id, 8 a request

    @invariant FurtherIsAlwaysNext
        -- A pager's next always leads further into its list, whatever
        -- relation the server files that direction under.

    @invariant TagFeedWorksAgainstBothSchemes
        -- The tag pager follows the Link header when there is one and
        -- asks by max_id when there is not. Against 0.15 the list ends
        -- with one request that comes back empty (KnownIssue
        -- tag_feed_extra_request).

    @invariant EveryReadAsksForThePixelfedEntity
        -- Every status and account read carries _pe=1, except favourites,
        -- which ignores it, and the discover endpoints, which always
        -- answer with the Pixelfed entity.
}

-- Pixelfed.Client: the routes that are not lists.
contract PixelfedApi {
    verify_credentials: () -> Account                           -- GET  /api/v1/accounts/verify_credentials?_pe=1
    update_credentials: (display_name: String, note: String, website: String, locked: Boolean) -> Account
                                                                -- POST /api/v1/accounts/update_credentials?_pe=1
    account: (id: String) -> Account                            -- GET  /api/v1/accounts/{id}?_pe=1
    relationship: (id: String) -> Relationship                  -- GET  /api/v1/accounts/relationships?id[]={id}&_pe=1
    account_action: (id: String, verb: String) -> Relationship  -- POST /api/v1/accounts/{id}/{follow|unfollow|block|unblock|mute|unmute}
    follow_request_action: (id: String, verb: String) -> Relationship
                                                                -- POST /api/v1/follow_requests/{id}/{authorize|reject}
    status: (id: String) -> Status                              -- GET  /api/v1/statuses/{id}?_pe=1
    context: (id: String) -> Json                               -- GET  /api/v1/statuses/{id}/context?_pe=1
    status_action: (id: String, verb: String) -> Status         -- POST /api/v1/statuses/{id}/{favourite|unfavourite|bookmark|unbookmark|reblog|unreblog}?_pe=1
    reply: (parent: String, text: String) -> Status             -- POST /api/v1/statuses?_pe=1
    create: (caption: String, media_ids: List<String>, visibility: Visibility, sensitive: Boolean, spoiler_text: String, comments_disabled: Boolean) -> Status
                                                                -- POST /api/v1/statuses?_pe=1
    edit: (id: String, caption: String, sensitive: Boolean, spoiler_text: String, media_ids: List<String>) -> Status
                                                                -- PUT  /api/v1/statuses/{id}
    delete: (id: String) -> Boolean                             -- DELETE /api/v1/statuses/{id}
    search: (query: String) -> Json                             -- GET  /api/v2/search?q=&_pe=1&resolve=1
    trending_posts: (range: TrendingRange) -> Json              -- GET  /api/v1.1/discover/posts/trending?range=
    popular_accounts: () -> Json                                -- GET  /api/v1.1/discover/accounts/popular
    trending_tags: () -> Json                                   -- GET  /api/v1.1/discover/posts/hashtags
    tag: (name: String) -> Hashtag                              -- GET  /api/v1/tags/{name}?_pe=1
    tag_action: (name: String, verb: String) -> Hashtag         -- POST /api/v1/tags/{name}/{follow|unfollow}
    send_message: (to: String, text: String) -> Message         -- POST /api/v1.1/direct/thread/send
    delete_message: (id: String) -> Boolean                     -- DELETE /api/v1.1/direct/thread/message?id=
    report: (object_type: String, object_id: String, reason: ReportReason, note: String) -> Boolean
                                                                -- POST /api/v1.1/report
    compose_settings: () -> ComposeSettings                     -- GET  /api/v1.1/compose/settings
    media_update: (id: String, description: String) -> MediaAttachment
                                                                -- PUT  /api/v1/media/{id}

    @invariant SpoilerOnlyWhenSensitive
        -- create sends spoiler_text only when it is non-empty after
        -- trimming, and the composer hands it over only for a sensitive
        -- post. edit always sends it, empty for a post that is not
        -- sensitive, so that turning the flag off clears the warning.

    @invariant EditSendsEveryAttachment
        -- edit's media_ids is the edited post's own list, complete and in
        -- order (D30).

    @guidance
        -- Routes pixelfed-rn uses that are not here are the NOT BUILT
        -- surfaces: /api/v1.2/stories/*, /api/v1.1/collections/*,
        -- /api/admin/*, /api/v1.1/push/*, /api/v1/domain_blocks,
        -- statuses/{id}/history, the avatar form of update_credentials,
        -- /api/v1.1/direct/compose/mutuals and thread/media.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Enumerations
------------------------------------------------------------

enum Method { GET | POST | PUT | DELETE }

-- decode is raised only by the UI's own decoders.
enum ErrorKind {
    no_session | invalid_domain | network | http | protocol
    | unsupported | storage | login_aborted | decode
}

-- other keeps a value the client does not know; the decoders hold the
-- server's own string beside it (D8).
enum Visibility { public | unlisted | private | direct | draft | other_visibility }

enum PfType {
    photo | photo_album | video | video_album | photo_video_album
    | share | text | other_type
}

enum MediaType { image | video_media | gifv | audio | unknown_media }

-- NotificationTransformer::replaceTypeVerb output; unknown verbs kept.
enum NotificationKind {
    follow | mention | shared | favourite | comment | tagged | modlog
    | direct_message | story_react | story_comment | other_verb
}

-- Hash routes. The first six are the tabs' own routes; public sits under
-- the Home tab. Every route starts with its own first segment: #/,
-- #/public, #/explore, #/compose, #/notifications, #/me, #/profile/{id},
-- #/status/{id}, #/tag/{name}, #/followers/{id}, #/following/{id},
-- #/liked-by/{id}, #/shared-by/{id}, #/bookmarks, #/likes, #/settings,
-- #/edit-profile, #/follow-requests, #/muted, #/blocked, #/followed-tags,
-- #/messages, #/thread/{id}, #/report-post/{id}, #/report-account/{id},
-- #/edit-post/{id}.
enum RouteKind {
    home | public_timeline | explore | compose | notifications | me
    | profile | status_detail | tag_feed | followers | following
    | liked_by | shared_by | bookmarks | likes | settings | edit_profile
    | follow_requests | muted | blocked | followed_tags | conversations
    | thread | report_post | report_account | edit_post
}

enum ListKind {
    home_feed | public_feed | bookmarks_feed | likes_feed | tag_posts
    | profile_posts | notification_rows | follower_rows | following_rows
    | liked_by_rows | shared_by_rows | muted_rows | blocked_rows
    | request_rows | followed_tag_rows | conversation_rows | message_rows
}

enum Toggle { favourite_toggle | bookmark_toggle | share_toggle }

enum SegmentKind { plain | tag_link | mention_link }

enum TrendingRange { daily | monthly | yearly }

-- ApiV1Dot1Controller::REPORT_TYPES.
enum ReportReason {
    spam | sensitive_content | abusive | underage | violence
    | copyright | impersonation | scam | terrorism
}

-- What a row's button does in a list of accounts.
enum RowAction { unmute_row | unblock_row | accept_row | reject_row }

-- A change to how the viewer stands to an account.
enum RelationChange { toggle_follow | toggle_mute | unblock_account | block_account }

enum IssueStatus { open | closed }

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entities
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Rust side only (D3).
entity Session {
    domain: Domain
    client_id: String
    client_secret: String
    access_token: String
    refresh_token: String?
    account_id: String
    acct: String
}

-- A login that has begun: the port is bound, the client registered, the
-- browser opened, the code not yet received.
entity PendingLogin {
    domain: Domain
    client_id: String
    client_secret: String
    redirect_uri: String
    state: String
    pkce: Pkce
    authorize_url: String
}

-- The one object the shell owns.
entity Core {
    session: Session?
    pending: PendingLogin?
}

-- Component.Root.
entity App {
    status: booting | boot_failed | logged_out | logged_in
    boot_error: String when status = boot_failed
    session: SessionSummary when status = logged_in
    -- The route in the address bar, kept while nobody is logged in.
    wanted: Route
    next_key: Integer
    screens: Screen with app = this

    transitions status {
        booting -> boot_failed
        booting -> logged_out
        booting -> logged_in
        logged_out -> logged_in
        logged_in -> logged_out
        terminal: boot_failed
    }

    depth: screens.count
}

-- Component.Login.
entity LoginForm {
    status: entering | working | waiting | login_failed
    error: AppError when status = login_failed
    authorize_url: String when status = waiting

    transitions status {
        entering -> working
        login_failed -> working
        working -> waiting
        working -> login_failed
        waiting -> login_failed
        waiting -> entering
        -- The two edges below exist only because an abandoned login stays
        -- live in Rust (KnownIssue abandoned_login_stays_live).
        entering -> login_failed
        login_failed -> entering
        terminal: entering
    }
}

-- One mounted screen (App.Stack.Entry). position counts from the tab's
-- own screen at 0; the screen with the highest position is in front and
-- is the only one displayed. key identifies the component instance and
-- is never reused.
entity Screen {
    app: App
    route: Route
    key: Integer
    position: Integer
    scroll: Integer
    in_front: Boolean
    notice: String?
    lists: PagedList with screen = this
    posts: PostView with screen = this
}

-- A list fetched a chunk at a time (App.Paged). Every paginated screen
-- holds one, the profile holds one for its grid and the thread one for
-- its messages.
entity PagedList {
    screen: Screen
    kind: ListKind
    status: first_loading | first_failed | idle | loading_more | more_failed | exhausted
    keys: List<String>
    error: AppError when status = first_failed | more_failed
    -- True while the server offers a chunk behind the last one held.
    has_next: Boolean

    transitions status {
        first_loading -> idle
        first_loading -> exhausted
        first_loading -> first_failed
        first_failed -> first_loading
        idle -> loading_more
        idle -> first_loading
        loading_more -> idle
        loading_more -> exhausted
        loading_more -> more_failed
        loading_more -> first_loading
        more_failed -> loading_more
        more_failed -> first_loading
        exhausted -> first_loading
        terminal: exhausted
    }

    wants_more: status = idle or status = more_failed
}

-- A post as one screen shows it: a card in a feed, a tile in a grid, the
-- main post of a detail screen or a comment under it.
entity PostView {
    screen: Screen
    post: Status
    busy: Boolean
    revealed: Boolean
}

-- Component.StatusDetail's own state beside its posts.
entity Detail {
    screen: Screen
    status_id: String
    main: pending_main | missing_main | ready_main
    comments: pending_comments | missing_comments | ready_comments
    -- The deletion of the main post: nothing asked, asked, being sent.
    status: not_armed | armed | deleting
    reply_text: String
    reply_sending: Boolean
    reply_error: String?
    is_mine: Boolean

    transitions status {
        not_armed -> armed
        armed -> not_armed
        armed -> deleting
        deleting -> not_armed
        terminal: not_armed
    }
}

-- Component.Profile's own state beside its grid.
entity ProfileView {
    screen: Screen
    account_id: String
    is_self: Boolean
    account: Account?
    relationship: Relationship?
    busy: Boolean
    block_armed: Boolean
}

-- Component.Feed's extra state for a hashtag feed.
entity TagHead {
    screen: Screen
    name: String
    info: Hashtag?
    busy: Boolean
}

-- Component.Explore.
entity Explore {
    screen: Screen
    query: String
    -- The search: none, out, answered, failed.
    status: not_searching | searching | found | search_failed
    searched_for: String when status = searching | found | search_failed
    range: TrendingRange
    posts_loaded: Boolean

    transitions status {
        not_searching -> searching
        searching -> found
        searching -> search_failed
        searching -> not_searching
        found -> searching
        found -> not_searching
        search_failed -> searching
        search_failed -> not_searching
        terminal: not_searching
    }
}

-- A form that sends one request: the profile editor, the post editor and
-- the report form.
entity Form {
    screen: Screen
    kind: profile_editor | post_editor | report_form
    status: editing | sending | sent | failed
    error: String when status = failed

    transitions status {
        editing -> sending
        sending -> sent
        sending -> failed
        failed -> sending
        failed -> editing
        sent -> editing
        terminal: sent
    }
}

-- Component.Thread's own state beside its messages.
entity ThreadView {
    screen: Screen
    other_account_id: String
    draft: String
    sending: Boolean
    send_error: String?
}

-- One picked file in the composer.
entity ComposeItem {
    composer: Composer
    key: Integer
    name: String
    mime: String
    size_bytes: Integer
    status: uploading | uploaded | rejected
    attachment: MediaAttachment when status = uploaded
    reason: String when status = rejected
    alt_text: String
    alt_saved: String
    alt_busy: Boolean

    transitions status {
        uploading -> uploaded
        uploading -> rejected
        terminal: uploaded, rejected
    }
}

-- Component.Compose.
entity Composer {
    screen: Screen
    settings: ComposeSettings
    caption: String
    visibility: Visibility
    sensitive: Boolean
    spoiler_text: String
    comments_disabled: Boolean
    status: composing | posting_now | post_failed
    post_error: String when status = post_failed
    items: ComposeItem with composer = this

    transitions status {
        composing -> posting_now
        post_failed -> posting_now
        posting_now -> post_failed
        posting_now -> composing
        post_failed -> composing
        terminal: composing
    }

    uploaded_items: items where status = uploaded
    unfinished_items: items where status != uploaded
    can_post: uploaded_items.count > 0 and unfinished_items.count = 0 and status != posting_now
}

-- Component.Settings.
entity SettingsView {
    screen: Screen
    logout_armed: Boolean
}

entity KnownIssue {
    name: String
    status: IssueStatus
    effect: String
    closes_when: String
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Config
------------------------------------------------------------

config {
    min_pixelfed_version: String = "0.12.3"
    min_pellucid_version: String = "0.1.0"
    scopes: String = "read write follow push"
    client_name: String = "Pellucid"
    client_website: String = "https://harryprayiv.com"
    identifier: String = "com.harryprayiv.pellucid"
    request_timeout: Duration = 30.seconds
    login_timeout: Duration = 10.minutes
    max_redirects: Integer = 5
    feed_page: Integer = 20
    profile_page: Integer = 24
    account_list_page: Integer = 20
    mute_block_page: Integer = 40
    followed_tags_page: Integer = 100
    thread_page: Integer = 8                  -- the server's own fixed size
    session_file: String = "session.json"
    session_file_mode: String = "0600"
    max_upload_bytes: Integer = 536_870_912   -- 512 MiB, Rust's ceiling before the instance's own
    pkce_verifier_bytes: Integer = 32
    max_stack_depth: Integer = 12             -- D24
    scroll_margin_px: Integer = 800           -- D26
    -- D32: the server's validation rules, the lower where versions differ.
    max_spoiler_length: Integer = 140
    max_search_length: Integer = 100
    max_display_name_length: Integer = 30
    max_note_length: Integer = 200
    max_website_length: Integer = 120
    max_message_length: Integer = 500
    max_report_note_length: Integer = 255
    -- Pixelfed's stock values, used when compose_settings cannot be read.
    default_allowed_media_types: List<String> = [ "image/jpeg", "image/jpg", "image/png", "image/gif" ]
    default_max_caption_length: Integer = 500
    default_max_file_size_kb: Integer = 15000
    default_max_media_attachments: Integer = 4
    default_max_alt_text_length: Integer = 1000
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Defaults
------------------------------------------------------------

default KnownIssue no_token_revoke = {
    name: "logout does not revoke the token on the server",
    status: open,
    effect: "a token copied out of session.json before logout stays valid until the instance expires it; the person can only revoke it from the instance's own settings page",
    closes_when: "the server offers a route that revokes the caller's own token. Stock Pixelfed does not; pellucid-server.allium rule TokenRevoked does"
}

default KnownIssue orphan_uploads = {
    name: "an upload removed from the composer, or abandoned with it, stays on the server",
    status: open,
    effect: "media uploaded and never attached to a status counts against the account's daily upload limit and storage until Pixelfed's garbage collector removes it",
    closes_when: "removing an uploaded item deletes it where the instance supports that, and leaving the composer with uploads asks first"
}

default KnownIssue smoke_harness_external = {
    name: "the headless UI run is not in the repository",
    status: open,
    effect: "scripts/check.fish does not run it; the 122 checks that drive every screen against a mock of contract Shell exist only where the port was written, so a change can pass the gate and break a screen. The run is JavaScript on jsdom, which is why it was not delivered",
    closes_when: "the screens' transitions are pure functions tested by spago test, as App.Paged and App.Stack already are, or a DOM driver that needs no npm package runs the bundle"
}

default KnownIssue mobile_store_missing = {
    name: "no SecretStore for Android or iOS",
    status: open,
    effect: "the mobile shells cannot persist a session",
    closes_when: "a Kotlin and a Swift store behind the SecretStore trait, exercised by the same round-trip test FileStore has"
}

default KnownIssue deep_link_unwritten = {
    name: "the mobile redirect branch of D10 is not written",
    status: open,
    effect: "a phone build cannot complete login; the loopback listener is unreachable from a system browser on Android and iOS",
    closes_when: "tauri-plugin-deep-link registers a scheme, the redirect URI registered in /api/v1/apps is that scheme on mobile, and on_open_url hands the code and state to login_finish"
}

default KnownIssue android_shell_untested = {
    name: "the android devShell has never been entered",
    status: open,
    effect: "SDK, NDK and build-tools versions in flake.nix are a first guess",
    closes_when: "cargo tauri android init and cargo tauri android dev succeed from that shell on winsmuth"
}

default KnownIssue lab_instance_undeployed = {
    name: "the client has spoken to a running server for a login and one timeline request only",
    status: open,
    effect: "every fact in this file but one comes from reading Pixelfed's source, and every screen has run to the end only against a mock of contract Shell. On 2026-11-10 a login to a real account succeeded and the first timeline request failed to decode (KnownIssue uncast_fields_failed_the_timeline). A fact read wrongly surfaces on the first real request that depends on it",
    closes_when: "the lab module is deployed on blade, a user created with pixelfed-manage, and login, a timeline, an upload, a post, a search and a direct message have each been done from Pellucid against it"
}

default KnownIssue tag_feed_extra_request = {
    name: "a hashtag feed ends with one empty request against Pixelfed 0.15",
    status: open,
    effect: "after the last page, which carries no Link header, the client asks once by max_id and receives []",
    closes_when: "the client reads the instance version once and picks the scheme, or stops when a page is shorter than the limit"
}

default KnownIssue likes_list_is_one_page_for_others = {
    name: "who liked and who shared stop at one page unless the viewer wrote the post",
    status: open,
    effect: "the server sends the Link header to the author only, so everyone else sees at most the first 20 accounts",
    closes_when: "a server that pages these lists for everyone allowed to see them; pellucid-server.allium does"
}

default KnownIssue conversations_start_from_a_profile = {
    name: "no recipient picker for a new conversation",
    status: open,
    effect: "a conversation with someone new starts from that person's profile; the Messages screen lists existing conversations only",
    closes_when: "a picker over /api/v1.1/direct/compose/mutuals and the search endpoint"
}

default KnownIssue abandoned_login_stays_live = {
    name: "pressing Reset on the waiting screen does not cancel the login in Rust",
    status: open,
    effect: "the loopback listener stays bound and the login task keeps waiting for up to ten minutes. A redirect that arrives in that time still logs in, and a timeout still shows its error on the form the person went back to. Starting a second login leaves two tasks waiting; whichever finishes last decides the session",
    closes_when: "login_start keeps a handle on the task it spawned and aborts it when a new login starts or a login_cancel command is called, and Reset calls that command"
}

default KnownIssue spec_unchecked = {
    name: "this file was never run through the Allium checker",
    status: closed,
    effect: "revisions one to three carried 301 checker errors; the spec could not catch an inconsistency in itself",
    closes_when: "allium check reports no errors. Closed 2026-11-10 by the rewrite"
}

default KnownIssue tauri_shell_uncompiled = {
    name: "src-tauri was reviewed against crate sources, not compiled",
    status: closed,
    effect: "a typo in src-tauri surfaced on the first cargo tauri dev rather than before delivery",
    closes_when: "cargo clippy -p pellucid -- -D warnings runs clean. Closed 2026-11-10: clean on winsmuth and where the port is written, against WebKitGTK 2.52"
}

default KnownIssue feeds_end_in_a_button = {
    name: "no infinite scroll",
    status: closed,
    effect: "each feed and the profile grid stopped at a Load more button",
    closes_when: "scrolling near the end of the page fetches the next chunk. Closed 2026-11-10 by D26"
}

default KnownIssue rename_reached_the_nodeinfo_check = {
    name: "the rename to Pellucid changed the server name the core accepts",
    status: closed,
    effect: "instance.rs compared nodeinfo's software.name with pellucid, so every Pixelfed server was refused at the probe with Unsupported server before login began. No test covered the comparison and every UI run mocked the shell, so the gate passed. domain.rs also suggested pellucid.social in its error messages",
    closes_when: "the comparison is against SERVER_SOFTWARE = pixelfed in a function with no network, and a unit test refuses the app's own name. Closed 2026-11-10; found by reading instance.rs after the first cargo tauri dev, not by the spec check, which had been done without that file"
}

default KnownIssue uncast_fields_failed_the_timeline = {
    name: "a flag sent as a number failed the whole home timeline",
    status: closed,
    effect: "the decoders read every optional field with one type in mind and failed the value on any other. MediaTransformer sends is_nsfw as the database holds it, so the first attachment of the first post failed its post, the post failed the page, and the home screen of a real account showed a decode error in place of the feed. The fixtures had been written with true and false where the server sends 0 and 1, so 162 checks and the headless run passed",
    closes_when: "every field that does not identify its entity is read by a reader that cannot fail (D8), the fixtures carry is_nsfw as 0, 1 and null and a tagged status_id as a bare number, and a post reduced to its id and account decodes. Closed 2026-11-10; found by Harry on the first real login, not by any check here. Putting the strict read back fails the suite"
}

default KnownIssue video_playback_unseen = {
    name: "no video has been seen playing in the desktop shell",
    status: open,
    effect: "the dev shell listed no GStreamer plugin, so what the webview could play depended on plugins the host session exported, and WebKit logged a missing WebVTT encoder once per feed video. The flake now lists the plugins and sets their path. That change was parsed and its attributes evaluated against the locked nixpkgs. It has not been built or run, and nobody has yet watched a video play",
    closes_when: "from the dev shell on winsmuth, cargo tauri dev no longer prints the WebVTT line and a video in the home feed plays with sound"
}

default KnownIssue client_refuses_this_server = {
    name: "the client has not signed in to a Pellucid server",
    status: open,
    effect: "check_software accepts the name pellucid (D33), and a development build reaches a server on its own machine (D34). On 2026-11-11, where this spec is written, the debug binary of the desktop shell signed in to a pellucid-server at http://127.0.0.1:8080 through its own login screen and showed the feeds, a profile, a follow and a post with their pictures; uploads and posts went through the core (status RUN). What is left: the same on winsmuth with a real browser and a file chosen in the composer, and a release build, which is https only (D5), trusts the public certificate authorities compiled into it and no others, and so needs a deployed server, of which there is none",
    closes_when: "a session against a deployed pellucid-server has signed in, posted a photo and read it back. The same entry is in pellucid-server.allium"
}

default KnownIssue back_on_first_screen_did_nothing = {
    name: "going back to the first screen of a restarted app changed the address and nothing else",
    status: closed,
    effect: "the app starts with an empty hash, which the route codec does not read as home, so the hashchange back to it was ignored and the screen in front stayed",
    closes_when: "parseRoute reads the empty hash as home. Closed 2026-11-10 by D31; found by the headless run"
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Session ----------------------------------------------------------------

rule AppLaunched {
    when: ProcessStarted(_)
    ensures:
        App.created(status: booting, wanted: home_route(), next_key: 0)
        LoginForm.created(status: entering)

    @guidance
        -- The one App and the one LoginForm there are, as the webview
        -- loads the bundle. Everything below operates on these two.
}

rule SessionRestored {
    when: AppStarted(_, stored, hash)
    requires: app.status = booting
    requires: stored != null
    let route = parse_route(hash)
    ensures:
        core.session = stored
        app.status = logged_in
        app.session = summary_of(stored)
        app.wanted = route
        Screen.created(app: app, route: route, key: app.next_key, position: 0, scroll: 0, in_front: true)
        app.next_key = app.next_key + 1

    @guidance
        -- Root subscribes to session-changed, to hash changes and to
        -- window scroll before it asks for the session, so nothing emitted
        -- during boot is missed. The first screen is the one the address
        -- bar names; an unknown hash and the empty hash are home (D31).
}

rule StartedLoggedOut {
    when: AppStarted(_, stored, hash)
    requires: app.status = booting
    requires: stored = null
    ensures:
        app.status = logged_out
        app.wanted = parse_route(hash)

    @guidance
        -- stored is null when there is no session file and also when
        -- there is one that cannot be read (CoreApi
        -- UnreadableSessionIsNoSession).
}

rule BootFailed {
    when: SessionUnanswered(_, message)
    requires: app.status = booting
    ensures:
        app.status = boot_failed
        app.boot_error = message

    @guidance
        -- The shell did not answer session_get. The one state with no
        -- button: the fix is outside the app. Until 2026-11-11 this rule
        -- was written for an unreadable session file, which the shell
        -- could never bring this far: its setup failed first.
}

rule LoginStarted {
    when: LoginSubmitted(_, domain_text)
    requires: app.status = logged_out
    requires: login.status = entering or login.status = login_failed
    requires: trimmed(domain_text) != ""
    ensures:
        login.status = working
        login.error = null
        LoginBegun(domain_text: domain_text)
}

rule BrowserOpened {
    when: LoginBegun(domain_text)
    requires: login.status = working
    let domain = parse_domain(domain_text)
    let server = Instance{domain: domain}
    requires: exists server
    requires: (server.software = "pixelfed" and version_at_least(server.version, config.min_pixelfed_version)) or (server.software = "pellucid" and version_at_least(server.version, config.min_pellucid_version))
    let pkce = fresh_pkce()
    ensures:
        let pending = PendingLogin.created(
            domain: domain,
            client_id: registered_client_id(domain),
            client_secret: registered_client_secret(domain),
            redirect_uri: loopback_redirect_uri(),
            state: fresh_uuid(),
            pkce: pkce,
            authorize_url: authorize_url_for(domain, pkce)
        )
        core.pending = pending
        ConsentPageOpened(url: pending.authorize_url)
        login.status = waiting
        login.authorize_url = pending.authorize_url

    @guidance
        -- server is the instance the parsed domain names, as its nodeinfo
        -- describes it. ConsentPageOpened is the operating system's
        -- browser showing the instance's own consent page; the app never
        -- embeds a login page. In order: the domain is parsed, nodeinfo is
        -- probed (software pixelfed or pellucid, at that kind's
        -- minimum version or newer, D33), a listener is
        -- bound on 127.0.0.1:0, a client is registered with that port as its
        -- redirect URI, and the authorize URL (client_id,
        -- redirect_uri, response_type=code, scope, state, code_challenge,
        -- code_challenge_method=S256) is opened in the system browser.
        -- Any of these failing is rule LoginRefused. The waiting screen
        -- shows the URL as text for the case where no browser opened.
}

rule LoginRefused {
    when: LoginBeginFailed(_, error)
    requires: login.status = working
    ensures:
        login.status = login_failed
        login.error = error
}

rule LoginCompleted {
    when: RedirectReceived(_, state, code)
    requires: app.status = logged_out
    requires: core.pending != null
    requires: state = core.pending.state and code != ""
    let token = exchange_code(core.pending, code)
    let account = verify_credentials(token)
    ensures:
        let session = Session.created(
            domain: core.pending.domain,
            client_id: core.pending.client_id,
            client_secret: core.pending.client_secret,
            access_token: token.access_token,
            refresh_token: token.refresh_token,
            account_id: account.id,
            acct: account.acct
        )
        core.session = session
        core.pending = null
        login.status = entering
        login.authorize_url = null
        app.status = logged_in
        app.session = summary_of(session)
        app.wanted = home_route()
        Screen.created(app: app, route: home_route(), key: app.next_key, position: 0, scroll: 0, in_front: true)
        app.next_key = app.next_key + 1

    @guidance
        -- The token request carries code, client_id, client_secret,
        -- redirect_uri, scope and code_verifier. The session is saved
        -- through SecretStore before session-changed is emitted. A request
        -- to the listener with the wrong state, another path or another
        -- method is answered 404 and the listener keeps waiting; the code
        -- is used once. The rule does not ask which login phase the form
        -- is in: a redirect that arrives after the person pressed Reset
        -- still logs in (KnownIssue abandoned_login_stays_live).
}

rule LoginFailed {
    when: LoginTaskFailed(_, error)
    requires: app.status = logged_out
    requires: login.status != working
    ensures:
        core.pending = null
        login.status = login_failed
        login.authorize_url = null
        login.error = error

    @guidance
        -- The timeout (login_timeout without a redirect), an error
        -- parameter on the redirect, a refused token exchange, a failed
        -- verify_credentials and a store that cannot be written. No
        -- session file and no partial session are left behind. After a
        -- Reset the form is back at entering and the failure of the
        -- abandoned login still lands on it, up to login_timeout later.
}

rule LoginAbandoned {
    when: LoginReset(_)
    requires: login.status = waiting
    ensures:
        login.status = entering
        login.authorize_url = null

    @guidance
        -- Only the form goes back. core.pending is untouched: the
        -- listener stays bound and the registered client stays usable
        -- until the redirect arrives or login_timeout passes.
}

rule LoggedOut {
    when: LogoutConfirmed(_, settings)
    requires: app.status = logged_in
    requires: settings.logout_armed
    ensures:
        core.session = null
        app.status = logged_out
        app.session = null
        app.wanted = home_route()
        for s in app.screens:
            not exists s

    @guidance
        -- The store is cleared, then session-changed is emitted with null.
        -- When clearing fails the UI still moves to logged_out: the file
        -- could not be removed, which is reported, but the person asked
        -- to leave. KnownIssue no_token_revoke.
}

-- Transport --------------------------------------------------------------

rule RequestSent {
    when: ApiRequested(_, request)
    requires: core.session != null
    requires: starts_with(request.path, "/api/")
    ensures: RequestOnTheWire(method: request.method, url: url_on(core.session.domain, request.path, request.query), bearer: core.session.access_token)

    @guidance
        -- Headers: Authorization Bearer, Accept application/json; the body
        -- as JSON when present. The answer is ApiResponse with next and
        -- prev from the Link header, AppError http when the status is not
        -- 2xx, AppError protocol when the body is not JSON. No session:
        -- no_session before any network activity. A path outside /api/:
        -- protocol, before any network activity.
}

rule CursorFollowed {
    when: CursorDereferenced(_, cursor)
    requires: core.session != null
    requires: same_origin(cursor.url, core.session.domain)
    requires: starts_with(path_of(cursor.url), "/api/")
    ensures: RequestOnTheWire(method: GET, url: cursor.url, bearer: core.session.access_token)

    @guidance
        -- same_origin compares scheme, host and port with the session
        -- domain's base URL, whose scheme is https outside D34. A cursor
        -- that fails the check is protocol with the offending URL in the
        -- message. The UI never builds or edits a cursor.
}

-- Navigation (App.Stack) -------------------------------------------------

rule RouteRemembered {
    when: HashChanged(_, route)
    requires: app.status != logged_in
    ensures: app.wanted = route
}

rule SteppedBack {
    when: HashChanged(_, route)
    requires: app.status = logged_in
    let front = front_screen(app)
    let beneath = screen_beneath(app)
    requires: front.route != route
    requires: beneath != null and beneath.route = route
    ensures:
        not exists front
        beneath.in_front = true
        app.wanted = route
        ScrollRestored(position: beneath.scroll)

    @guidance
        -- The screen that was in front is unmounted and its state is
        -- gone. The one underneath is displayed as it was left; nothing is
        -- fetched.
}

rule TabSwitched {
    when: HashChanged(_, route)
    requires: app.status = logged_in
    let front = front_screen(app)
    let beneath = screen_beneath(app)
    requires: front.route != route
    requires: beneath = null or beneath.route != route
    requires: is_tab_route(route)
    ensures:
        for s in app.screens:
            not exists s
        Screen.created(app: app, route: route, key: app.next_key, position: 0, scroll: 0, in_front: true)
        app.next_key = app.next_key + 1
        app.wanted = route
        ScrollRestored(position: 0)

    @guidance
        -- The tab routes are home, public_timeline, explore, compose,
        -- notifications and me. Home and Public are two routes under one
        -- tab; switching between them replaces the stack like any other
        -- tab switch.
}

rule SteppedForward {
    when: HashChanged(_, route)
    requires: app.status = logged_in
    let front = front_screen(app)
    let beneath = screen_beneath(app)
    requires: front.route != route
    requires: beneath = null or beneath.route != route
    requires: not is_tab_route(route)
    ensures:
        front.in_front = false
        front.scroll = current_scroll()
        Screen.created(app: app, route: route, key: app.next_key, position: front.position + 1, scroll: 0, in_front: true)
        app.next_key = app.next_key + 1
        app.wanted = route
        ScrollRestored(position: 0)
        if app.depth > config.max_stack_depth:
            StackOverfull(app: app)

    @guidance
        -- A route equal to the one two screens down is a step forward,
        -- not two steps back: hash routing reports the address, not the
        -- direction.
}

rule StackTrimmed {
    when: StackOverfull(app)
    let oldest = screen_at(app, 1)
    requires: oldest != null
    ensures:
        not exists oldest
        for s in app.screens where position > 1:
            s.position = s.position - 1

    @guidance
        -- The tab's own screen, at position 0, is never dropped.
}

rule TabPressedAgain {
    when: TabPressed(_, route)
    requires: app.status = logged_in
    requires: front_screen(app).route = route
    ensures: ScrollRestored(position: 0)

    @guidance
        -- Pressing any other tab sets the hash, which is rule TabSwitched.
}

rule PageNearEnd {
    when: WindowScrolled(_)
    requires: app.status = logged_in
    requires: page_below_viewport() <= config.scroll_margin_px
    ensures:
        for list in front_screen(app).lists where wants_more and kind != message_rows:
            MoreRequested(list: list)

    @guidance
        -- Only the screen in front is told (D26). The thread's messages
        -- grow upwards, towards earlier ones, and are fetched by their own
        -- button.
}

-- The paging machine (App.Paged) -----------------------------------------

rule ListRequested {
    when: ScreenOpened(_, screen, kind)
    ensures: PagedList.created(screen: screen, kind: kind, status: first_loading, keys: [], has_next: false)

    @guidance
        -- The first chunk is requested as the list is created. Which
        -- screens hold which lists: the five feeds one list of posts; the
        -- profile one for its grid; notifications, the seven account
        -- lists, followed hashtags and conversations one each; the thread
        -- one for its messages.
}

rule FirstChunkArrived {
    when: ChunkArrived(_, list, chunk)
    requires: list.status = first_loading
    ensures:
        list.keys = chunk.keys
        list.has_next = chunk.has_next
        if chunk.has_next and chunk.keys != []:
            list.status = idle
        else:
            list.status = exhausted
}

rule FirstChunkFailed {
    when: ChunkFailed(_, list, error)
    requires: list.status = first_loading
    ensures:
        list.status = first_failed
        list.error = error
}

rule ListReloaded {
    when: ReloadPressed(_, list)
    requires:
        list.status = first_failed or list.status = idle or list.status = loading_more
        or list.status = more_failed or list.status = exhausted
    ensures:
        list.status = first_loading
        list.error = null
        list.keys = []
        list.has_next = false

    @guidance
        -- From any state but first_loading, where a reload is already
        -- under way. An answer still out for the list as it was is
        -- dropped when it arrives: rules MoreArrived and MoreFailed
        -- require loading_more, and a first chunk for a source the screen
        -- has left is discarded by the screen.
}

rule MoreRequested {
    when: MoreRequested(list)
    requires: list.status = idle or list.status = more_failed
    ensures:
        list.status = loading_more
        list.error = null
}

rule MoreArrived {
    when: ChunkArrived(_, list, chunk)
    requires: list.status = loading_more
    let fresh = keys_not_held(chunk.keys, list.keys)
    ensures:
        list.keys = list.keys + fresh
        list.has_next = chunk.has_next
        if chunk.has_next and fresh != []:
            list.status = idle
        else:
            list.status = exhausted

    @guidance
        -- fresh is the chunk's keys that are not held yet, each once. A
        -- chunk with nothing new ends the list even when the server offers
        -- another cursor, which stops a loop on a server that repeats
        -- itself. Keys: a post by its id, an account by its id, a hashtag
        -- by its lower-cased name, a message and a conversation by its id.
}

rule MoreFailed {
    when: ChunkFailed(_, list, error)
    requires: list.status = loading_more
    ensures:
        list.status = more_failed
        list.error = error

    @guidance
        -- The items stay and the pager is kept, so the same chunk can be
        -- asked for again.
}

-- Changes that travel between screens (App.Screen) -----------------------

rule PostChangedEverywhere {
    when: PostChanged(post)
    ensures:
        for view in PostViews where post.id = post.id or post.reblog_of = post.id:
            view.post = replaced_displayed(view.post, post)

    @guidance
        -- Raised with the displayed post, never a share wrapper, after a
        -- toggle is merged, an edit is saved, or the main post's comment
        -- count moves. Every mounted feed, profile grid and detail screen
        -- replaces its copy, whether it holds the post itself or a share
        -- that wraps it.
}

rule PostRemovedEverywhere {
    when: PostRemoved(status_id)
    ensures:
        for view in PostViews where post.id = status_id or post.reblog_of = status_id:
            not exists view
}

rule AccountReloadedEverywhere {
    when: AccountChanged(account_id)
    ensures:
        for profile in ProfileViews where account_id = account_id:
            ProfileRefetched(profile: profile)
}

-- Posts ------------------------------------------------------------------

rule ToggleRequested {
    when: TogglePressed(_, view, toggle)
    requires: not view.busy
    requires: toggle != share_toggle or view.post.visibility = public
    ensures: view.busy = true

    @guidance
        -- The request flips the flag the post currently has: favourite or
        -- unfavourite, bookmark or unbookmark, reblog or unreblog. The
        -- card shows the old state while busy and disables its buttons.
        -- The share button is drawn only on a public post.
}

rule ToggleAnswered {
    when: ToggleAnswered(_, view, toggle, answer)
    requires: view.busy
    ensures:
        view.busy = false
        view.post = merged(toggle, view.post, answer)
        PostChanged(post: merged(toggle, view.post, answer))

    @guidance
        -- merged (Pixelfed.StatusOps.merge): favourite takes the server's
        -- copy whole; bookmark takes only bookmarked; share takes
        -- reblogged and moves reblogs_count by one when the flag flipped,
        -- not below zero (D9).
}

rule ToggleFailed {
    when: ToggleFailed(_, view, error)
    requires: view.busy
    ensures:
        view.busy = false
        view.screen.notice = error.message
}

rule SensitiveRevealed {
    when: ShowPressed(_, view)
    requires: view.post.sensitive
    ensures: view.revealed = true

    @guidance
        -- Media of a sensitive post is not requested until revealed.
}

rule CaptionLinkPressed {
    when: SegmentPressed(_, segment)
    requires: segment.kind != plain
    ensures:
        if segment.kind = tag_link:
            HashRequested(route: tag_route(segment.text))
        else:
            HashRequested(route: profile_route(segment.account_id))
}

rule DetailOpened {
    when: DetailLoaded(_, detail, main, viewer_id)
    requires: detail.main = pending_main
    ensures:
        detail.main = ready_main
        detail.is_mine = (main.account.id = viewer_id)
        PostView.created(screen: detail.screen, post: main, busy: false, revealed: false)

    @guidance
        -- The post and its context are fetched in parallel. Comments are
        -- the descendants, flat, in server order. The viewer's own post
        -- offers Edit and Delete in the header; anyone else's offers
        -- Report. A failed fetch leaves missing_main with Try again.
}

rule ReplySubmitted {
    when: ReplySubmitted(_, detail, text)
    requires: detail.main = ready_main
    requires: trimmed(text) != "" and not detail.reply_sending
    ensures:
        detail.reply_sending = true
        detail.reply_error = null
}

rule ReplyPosted {
    when: ReplyAnswered(_, detail, comment, main)
    requires: detail.reply_sending
    ensures:
        detail.reply_sending = false
        detail.reply_text = ""
        PostView.created(screen: detail.screen, post: comment, busy: false, revealed: false)
        PostChanged(post: with_reply_count(main, main.reply_count + 1))
}

rule CommentDeleted {
    when: CommentDeleteAnswered(_, detail, view, main)
    requires: view.busy
    ensures:
        not exists view
        PostChanged(post: with_reply_count(main, main.reply_count - 1))

    @guidance
        -- The delete button exists only on the viewer's own comments and
        -- sends at once; the count does not go below zero.
}

rule PostDeleteArmed {
    when: DeletePressed(_, detail)
    requires: detail.is_mine and detail.status = not_armed
    ensures: detail.status = armed
}

rule PostDeleteCancelled {
    when: KeepPressed(_, detail)
    requires: detail.status = armed
    ensures: detail.status = not_armed
}

rule PostDeleteConfirmed {
    when: ConfirmDeletePressed(_, detail)
    requires: detail.is_mine and detail.status = armed
    ensures: detail.status = deleting
}

rule PostDeleted {
    when: DeleteAnswered(_, detail)
    requires: detail.status = deleting
    ensures:
        PostRemoved(status_id: detail.status_id)
        BackRequested(app: app)

    @guidance
        -- Every screen still holding the post drops it, then the detail
        -- screen leaves through history.back(), which is rule SteppedBack.
}

rule PostDeleteFailed {
    when: DeleteFailed(_, detail, error)
    requires: detail.status = deleting
    ensures:
        detail.status = not_armed
        detail.screen.notice = error.message
}

-- Forms: profile editor, post editor, report -----------------------------

rule FormSubmitted {
    when: FormSubmitted(_, form)
    requires: form.status = editing or form.status = failed
    requires: form_is_valid(form)
    ensures:
        form.status = sending
        form.error = null

    @guidance
        -- Valid means: the profile editor's three fields within their
        -- limits; the post editor's caption within the instance's limit
        -- and the viewer the author of a post that is not a share; the
        -- report form with a reason chosen.
}

rule FormEdited {
    when: FormEdited(_, form)
    requires: form.status = failed or form.status = sent
    ensures:
        form.status = editing
        form.error = null

    @guidance
        -- Any edit takes back the Saved or failed line.
}

rule FormRejected {
    when: FormFailed(_, form, error)
    requires: form.status = sending
    ensures:
        form.status = failed
        form.error = error.message
}

rule ProfileSaved {
    when: FormAnswered(_, form, account_id)
    requires: form.status = sending and form.kind = profile_editor
    ensures:
        form.status = sent
        AccountChanged(account_id: account_id)

    @guidance
        -- Every field is sent, so clearing one clears it on the server.
        -- The server's copy replaces the form's: it trims and cleans.
}

rule PostEditSaved {
    when: EditAnswered(_, form, post)
    requires: form.status = sending and form.kind = post_editor
    ensures:
        form.status = sent
        PostChanged(post: post)
        BackRequested(app: app)

    @guidance
        -- The request carries the trimmed caption, the sensitive flag, the
        -- content warning (empty unless sensitive) and every media id the
        -- post has, in order (D30).
}

rule ReportAccepted {
    when: ReportAnswered(_, form)
    requires: form.status = sending and form.kind = report_form
    ensures: form.status = sent

    @guidance
        -- The body is report_type, object_type (post or user), object_id
        -- and, when the note is not empty, message. A 400 (own content, a
        -- duplicate, a note too long) is rule FormRejected with the
        -- server's words.
}

-- Hashtags ---------------------------------------------------------------

rule TagHeadLoaded {
    when: TagAnswered(_, head, info)
    ensures: head.info = info

    @guidance
        -- Fetched beside the feed's first chunk. A failure leaves the
        -- header without its count and without its button; the feed is
        -- unaffected.
}

rule TagFollowRequested {
    when: TagFollowPressed(_, head)
    requires: head.info != null and not head.busy
    ensures: head.busy = true

    @guidance
        -- Sends unfollow when the tag is followed and follow otherwise.
        -- The server refuses to follow a tag no post has used (422), which
        -- lands as a notice with busy cleared.
}

rule TagFollowToggled {
    when: TagFollowAnswered(_, head, following)
    requires: head.info != null and head.busy
    ensures:
        head.busy = false
        head.info = with_following(head.info, following)

    @guidance
        -- The answer to follow and unfollow carries no count, so the one
        -- held is kept.
}

-- Explore ----------------------------------------------------------------

rule SearchSubmitted {
    when: SearchSubmitted(_, explore, term)
    requires: explore.status != searching
    requires: trimmed(term) != ""
    ensures:
        explore.status = searching
        explore.searched_for = trimmed(term)
}

rule SearchAnswered {
    when: SearchAnswered(_, explore, term)
    requires: explore.status = searching and explore.searched_for = term
    ensures: explore.status = found

    @guidance
        -- The result is two lists, people and hashtags; the server returns
        -- no posts. An answer for a term other than the one being waited
        -- for is dropped.
}

rule SearchFailed {
    when: SearchFailed(_, explore, term)
    requires: explore.status = searching and explore.searched_for = term
    ensures: explore.status = search_failed
}

rule SearchCleared {
    when: ClearPressed(_, explore)
    requires: explore.status != not_searching
    ensures:
        explore.status = not_searching
        explore.searched_for = null
        explore.query = ""
}

rule RangeChanged {
    when: RangePicked(_, explore, range)
    requires: explore.range != range
    ensures:
        explore.range = range
        explore.posts_loaded = false

    @guidance
        -- Trending hashtags, popular accounts and trending posts load in
        -- parallel when the tab opens; a failure in one shows in its own
        -- section. Changing the range refetches the posts only, and an
        -- answer for a range the person has since left is dropped.
}

-- Profile ----------------------------------------------------------------

rule ProfileOpened {
    when: ProfileLoaded(_, profile, account, relationship)
    ensures:
        profile.account = account
        profile.relationship = relationship

    @guidance
        -- The account and, unless it is the viewer's own, the relationship
        -- are fetched in parallel; a relationship error is a notice, not a
        -- failure. The grid's first chunk follows the account. Also the
        -- effect of ProfileRefetched, which fetches the same again.
}

rule RelationChangeRequested {
    when: RelationPressed(_, profile, change)
    requires: profile.relationship != null and not profile.busy and not profile.is_self
    requires: change != block_account or profile.block_armed
    ensures: profile.busy = true

    @guidance
        -- toggle_follow sends unfollow when following or requested (which
        -- withdraws a request) and follow otherwise; toggle_mute sends
        -- unmute when muting and mute otherwise.
}

rule RelationAnswered {
    when: RelationAnswered(_, profile, relationship)
    requires: profile.busy
    ensures:
        profile.busy = false
        profile.block_armed = false
        profile.relationship = relationship
}

rule RelationFailed {
    when: RelationFailed(_, profile, error)
    requires: profile.busy
    ensures:
        profile.busy = false
        profile.block_armed = false
        profile.screen.notice = error.message
}

rule BlockArmed {
    when: BlockPressed(_, profile)
    requires: profile.relationship != null and not profile.relationship.blocking
    ensures: profile.block_armed = true
}

rule BlockDisarmed {
    when: BlockCancelled(_, profile)
    requires: profile.block_armed
    ensures: profile.block_armed = false
}

-- Account lists ----------------------------------------------------------

rule RowActionApplied {
    when: RowActionAnswered(_, list, account_id)
    requires: list.kind = muted_rows or list.kind = blocked_rows or list.kind = request_rows
    ensures: list.keys = keys_without(list.keys, account_id)

    @guidance
        -- Unmute on the muted list, Unblock on the blocked list, Accept
        -- and Reject on the follow requests; each takes the row out on
        -- success and leaves a notice on failure. Unfollow on the followed
        -- hashtags does the same for a hashtag row.
}

-- Direct messages --------------------------------------------------------

rule MessageSubmitted {
    when: MessageSubmitted(_, thread, text)
    requires: trimmed(text) != "" and not thread.sending
    ensures:
        thread.sending = true
        thread.send_error = null
}

rule MessageSent {
    when: MessageAnswered(_, thread, list, message_id)
    requires: thread.sending and list.kind = message_rows
    ensures:
        thread.sending = false
        thread.draft = ""
        list.keys = [ message_id ] + keys_without(list.keys, message_id)

    @guidance
        -- The list is held newest first, as the server sends it, and drawn
        -- oldest first. Only text is sent; photos and videos others sent
        -- are drawn. A message without created_at (0.12's answer to a
        -- send) shows the server's own age label.
}

rule MessageSendFailed {
    when: MessageFailed(_, thread, error)
    requires: thread.sending
    ensures:
        thread.sending = false
        thread.send_error = error.message
}

-- Notifications ----------------------------------------------------------

rule NotificationOpened {
    when: NotificationPressed(_, notification)
    let target = notification_target(notification)
    requires: target != null
    ensures: HashRequested(route: target)

    @guidance
        -- notification_target, first match: a direct message opens the
        -- thread with its sender; a tag that carries a tagged_status_id
        -- opens it; a comment
        -- opens its parent (in_reply_to_id, else the comment) so it is
        -- read in place; anything else with a post opens that post;
        -- anything else with an actor opens the actor; a row with neither
        -- is drawn disabled.
}

-- Compose ----------------------------------------------------------------

rule MediaPicked {
    when: FilePicked(_, composer, name, mime, size_bytes)
    requires: composer.items.count < composer.settings.max_media_attachments
    ensures:
        if size_bytes > composer.settings.max_file_size_kb * 1024:
            ComposeItem.created(composer: composer, key: fresh_item_key(composer), name: name, mime: mime, size_bytes: size_bytes, status: rejected, reason: "larger than the instance allows", alt_text: "", alt_saved: "", alt_busy: false)
        else:
            ComposeItem.created(composer: composer, key: fresh_item_key(composer), name: name, mime: mime, size_bytes: size_bytes, status: uploading, alt_text: "", alt_saved: "", alt_busy: false)

    @guidance
        -- A type the instance does not list is rejected the same way. The
        -- limits are the instance's (compose_settings) or, when that call
        -- fails, Pixelfed's stock defaults with a notice. An accepted file
        -- is read once, crosses the IPC once as a raw body and is never
        -- written to disk by the shell (D20).
}

rule MediaUploaded {
    when: UploadAnswered(_, item, attachment)
    requires: item.status = uploading
    ensures:
        item.status = uploaded
        item.attachment = attachment
}

rule MediaUploadFailed {
    when: UploadFailed(_, item, error)
    requires: item.status = uploading
    ensures:
        item.status = rejected
        item.reason = error.message
}

rule AltTextSaved {
    when: AltTextAnswered(_, item, description)
    requires: item.status = uploaded and item.alt_busy
    ensures:
        item.alt_busy = false
        item.alt_saved = description

    @guidance
        -- Sent with PUT /api/v1/media/{id} when the field loses focus and
        -- again, for anything still unsaved, before the post is created.
}

rule PostSubmitted {
    when: PostPressed(_, composer)
    requires: composer.can_post
    ensures:
        composer.status = posting_now
        composer.post_error = null
}

rule PostCreated {
    when: CreateAnswered(_, composer, status_id)
    requires: composer.status = posting_now
    ensures:
        composer.status = composing
        composer.caption = ""
        composer.visibility = start_visibility(composer.settings)
        composer.sensitive = false
        composer.spoiler_text = ""
        composer.comments_disabled = false
        for item in composer.items:
            not exists item
        HashRequested(route: status_route(status_id))

    @guidance
        -- The composer stays mounted under the post it leads to, so it is
        -- emptied here: coming back must not offer the same post again.
        -- start_visibility is the instance's default when that is public,
        -- unlisted or private, and public otherwise; the limits already
        -- fetched are kept.
}

rule PostCreateFailed {
    when: CreateFailed(_, composer, error)
    requires: composer.status = posting_now
    ensures:
        composer.status = post_failed
        composer.post_error = error.message
}

rule ComposerEdited {
    when: CaptionEdited(_, composer, text)
    requires: composer.status = post_failed
    ensures:
        composer.status = composing
        composer.post_error = null
        composer.caption = text
}

-- Settings ---------------------------------------------------------------

rule LogoutArmed {
    when: LogoutPressed(_, settings)
    requires: not settings.logout_armed
    ensures: settings.logout_armed = true
}

rule LogoutCancelled {
    when: StayPressed(_, settings)
    requires: settings.logout_armed
    ensures: settings.logout_armed = false
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants
------------------------------------------------------------

invariant OneScreenInFront {
    for a in Apps:
        a.status = logged_in implies (a.screens where in_front).count = 1
}

invariant NoScreensWithoutASession {
    for a in Apps:
        a.status != logged_in implies a.screens.count = 0
}

invariant StackIsBounded {
    for a in Apps:
        a.screens.count <= config.max_stack_depth
}

invariant ScreenKeysAreUnique {
    for a in Screens:
        for b in Screens:
            a != b implies a.key != b.key
}

invariant TheTabScreenIsAtTheBottom {
    for s in Screens:
        s.position >= 0
}

invariant ListsNeverRepeat {
    for l in PagedLists:
        is_duplicate_free(l.keys)
}

invariant ExhaustedListsOfferNothing {
    for l in PagedLists:
        l.status = idle implies l.has_next
}

invariant NoPostWithoutMedia {
    -- D21. The server's rule, held on the client so the 403 is never seen.
    for c in Composers:
        c.can_post implies c.uploaded_items.count > 0
}

invariant OnlyTheAuthorDeletes {
    for d in Details:
        d.status != not_armed implies d.is_mine
}

invariant ABusyListHasNoError {
    for l in PagedLists:
        l.status = first_loading or l.status = loading_more implies not l.wants_more
}

-- The properties below hold over requests, IPC messages and the DOM,
-- which are not entity state. They are stated on the contracts above
-- (TokenAbsent, ApiPathsOnly, CursorsValidated, UploadsBounded,
-- PkceAlways, Named) and repeated here as the list a reviewer checks:
--
--   TokenNeverCrossesTheBridge   no command result and no event payload
--                                contains the access token, the client
--                                secret, the refresh token or the PKCE
--                                verifier
--   TokenOnlyToApiPaths          every request carrying Authorization goes
--                                to the session's scheme, host and port,
--                                the scheme being https outside D34, and
--                                to a path under /api/
--   NoHtmlInjection              no node is set through innerHTML; a
--                                caption is text nodes and buttons
--   ForeignBudgetHeld            every .js file under src/ is listed in
--                                contract ForeignBudget
--   WarningFreeBuild             scripts/check.fish (D15)
--   BytesCrossOnce               a picked file is read once, sent once and
--                                never written by the shell

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Actor Declarations
------------------------------------------------------------

actor Viewer {
    identified_by: App where status != boot_failed
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Surfaces
------------------------------------------------------------

-- What reaches the app from outside the person: the operating system,
-- the webview and the instance's answers.
surface Platform {
    facing os: Core

    exposes:
        os.session != null
        os.pending != null

    provides:
        ProcessStarted(os)
        AppStarted(os, stored, hash)
        SessionUnanswered(os, message)
        HashChanged(os, route)
        WindowScrolled(os)
        RedirectReceived(os, state, code)

    @guidance
        -- HashChanged is also what HashRequested and BackRequested lead
        -- to: a screen sets the hash or calls history.back(), and the
        -- webview reports the new address.
}

surface InstanceAnswers {
    facing server: Instance

    exposes:
        server.domain
        server.software
        server.version
        InstanceProbe
        ApiResponse
        Chunk

    provides:
        LoginBeginFailed(server, error)
        LoginTaskFailed(server, error)
        ChunkArrived(server, list, chunk)
        ChunkFailed(server, list, error)
        ToggleAnswered(server, view, toggle, answer)
        ToggleFailed(server, view, error)
        DetailLoaded(server, detail, main, viewer_id)
        ReplyAnswered(server, detail, comment, main)
        CommentDeleteAnswered(server, detail, view, main)
        DeleteAnswered(server, detail)
        DeleteFailed(server, detail, error)
        FormFailed(server, form, error)
        FormAnswered(server, form, account_id)
        EditAnswered(server, form, post)
        ReportAnswered(server, form)
        TagAnswered(server, head, info)
        TagFollowAnswered(server, head, following)
        SearchAnswered(server, explore, term)
        SearchFailed(server, explore, term)
        ProfileLoaded(server, profile, account, relationship)
        RelationAnswered(server, profile, relationship)
        RelationFailed(server, profile, error)
        RowActionAnswered(server, list, account_id)
        MessageAnswered(server, thread, list, message_id)
        MessageFailed(server, thread, error)
        UploadAnswered(server, item, attachment)
        UploadFailed(server, item, error)
        AltTextAnswered(server, item, description)
        CreateAnswered(server, composer, status_id)
        CreateFailed(server, composer, error)

    contracts:
        demands PixelfedApi
        demands Pagers

    @guarantee AnswersAreData
        -- Nothing an instance sends is executed or rendered as markup. A
        -- body that does not decode is AppError decode, shown as text.

    @guarantee OnlyIdentityFailsADecode
        -- D8. A field that does not identify its entity cannot produce
        -- AppError decode, whatever type it arrives as. The error text
        -- names the path to the field that did: the index in the page,
        -- then each key.
}

-- What the UI asks of the shell. Every screen's request goes through
-- one of these two commands, or through media_upload from the composer.
surface Bridge {
    facing ui: App

    exposes:
        ui.next_key

    provides:
        ApiRequested(ui, request) when ui.status = logged_in
        CursorDereferenced(ui, cursor) when ui.status = logged_in

    contracts:
        demands Shell

    @guarantee TokenStaysInRust
        -- Contract Shell's TokenAbsent, seen from the page: what comes
        -- back over the bridge is decoded JSON and opaque cursors.
}

surface LoginScreen {
    facing viewer: Viewer

    exposes:
        login.status
        login.error when login.status = login_failed
        login.authorize_url when login.status = waiting

    provides:
        LoginSubmitted(viewer, domain_text) when login.status = entering or login.status = login_failed
        LoginReset(viewer) when login.status = waiting

    contracts:
        demands Shell
        demands CoreApi
        demands SecretStore

    @guarantee NoEmbeddedLogin
        -- The password is typed into the system browser on the instance's
        -- own page, never into the app.

    @guarantee NothingLeaksOnFailure
        -- A failed login leaves no session file and no partial session in
        -- memory; the registered client is abandoned on the server.
}

-- The signed-in shell: the stack of screens and the five tabs (Home,
-- Explore, Post, Alerts, Me).
surface SignedInShell {
    facing viewer: Viewer

    exposes:
        app.status
        app.boot_error when app.status = boot_failed
        app.session when app.status = logged_in
        app.wanted
        app.depth
        for screen in app.screens:
            screen.route
            screen.key
            screen.position
            screen.in_front
            screen.scroll
            screen.notice

    provides:
        TabPressed(viewer, route) when app.status = logged_in
        ScreenOpened(viewer, screen, kind) when app.status = logged_in

    contracts:
        demands Backend
        demands ForeignBudget

    @guarantee OnlyTheFrontScreenIsDisplayed
        -- Every mounted screen stays in the document; all but the one in
        -- front carry display: none.

    @guarantee BackFetchesNothing
        -- Going back shows the screen underneath as it was left, at the
        -- scroll position it was left at, without a request (D24).

    @guidance
        -- The Home tab is active on home and public_timeline. Screens are
        -- keyed elements, so the document moves no screen's nodes when
        -- another is pushed or popped.
}

-- Component.Feed: home, public, bookmarks, likes and a hashtag's feed.
surface TimelineScreen {
    facing viewer: Viewer
    context list: PagedList where kind in { home_feed, public_feed, bookmarks_feed, likes_feed, tag_posts }

    exposes:
        list.status
        list.keys
        list.has_next
        list.error when list.status = first_failed or list.status = more_failed
        for view in list.screen.posts:
            view.post
            view.busy
            view.revealed

        Toggle
        Segment

    provides:
        ReloadPressed(viewer, list)
        MoreRequested(list) when list.wants_more
        TogglePressed(viewer, view, toggle)
        ShowPressed(viewer, view)
        SegmentPressed(viewer, segment)

    contracts:
        demands Backend

    @guarantee CaptionsAreText
        -- A caption is drawn as text nodes and buttons (D6, D27).

    @guidance
        -- A card: share line, avatar, names, age and an edited mark, media
        -- or a sensitive cover, like with count, comments with count,
        -- share with count on a public post, bookmark, a line that opens
        -- who liked and who shared when either count is above zero,
        -- caption, place. Home and Public carry a two-way switch and the
        -- way into Messages; the others a back header. A hashtag feed adds
        -- the tag's post count and a Follow button (entity TagHead).
}

-- The head of a hashtag feed: its post count and the Follow button.
surface TagFeedHeader {
    facing viewer: Viewer
    context head: TagHead

    exposes:
        head.name
        head.info
        head.busy

    provides:
        TagFollowPressed(viewer, head) when head.info != null and not head.busy
}

-- Component.AccountList, Component.FollowedTags, Component.Conversations
-- and the list half of Component.Notifications and Component.Thread.
surface ListScreens {
    facing viewer: Viewer
    context list: PagedList where kind in { notification_rows, follower_rows, following_rows, liked_by_rows, shared_by_rows, muted_rows, blocked_rows, request_rows, followed_tag_rows, conversation_rows, message_rows, profile_posts }

    exposes:
        list.kind
        list.status
        list.keys
        list.has_next
        list.error when list.status = first_failed or list.status = more_failed
        RowAction
        Notification
        Conversation
        Message

    provides:
        ReloadPressed(viewer, list)
        MoreRequested(list) when list.wants_more

    contracts:
        demands Backend

    @guarantee RowsNeverRepeat
        -- A row appears once however the server pages (ListsNeverRepeat).

    @guidance
        -- An account row: avatar and names open the profile; the muted,
        -- blocked and follow request lists add their buttons on the
        -- right. A conversation is drawn by its first other participant
        -- and opens the thread with them; one with no readable
        -- participant is left out. Who liked and who shared stop at one
        -- page unless the viewer wrote the post (KnownIssue
        -- likes_list_is_one_page_for_others). The thread's list grows by
        -- its own Earlier messages button, not by scrolling.
}

surface PostDetailScreen {
    facing viewer: Viewer
    context detail: Detail

    exposes:
        detail.status_id
        detail.main
        detail.comments
        detail.status
        detail.reply_text
        detail.reply_sending
        detail.reply_error
        detail.is_mine

    provides:
        ReplySubmitted(viewer, detail, text) when detail.main = ready_main
        DeletePressed(viewer, detail) when detail.is_mine and detail.status = not_armed
        KeepPressed(viewer, detail) when detail.status = armed
        ConfirmDeletePressed(viewer, detail) when detail.status = armed

    @guidance
        -- The reply form is absent when the post has comments off. A
        -- comment row: avatar, name, age, text with the same links as a
        -- caption, like with count, delete on the viewer's own.
}

-- Component.EditProfile, Component.EditPost and Component.Report.
surface FormScreens {
    facing viewer: Viewer
    context form: Form

    exposes:
        form.kind
        form.status
        form.error when form.status = failed

    provides:
        FormSubmitted(viewer, form) when form.status = editing or form.status = failed
        FormEdited(viewer, form) when form.status = failed or form.status = sent

    @guarantee LimitsBeforeTheRequest
        -- Each field stops at the server's own limit (D32), so a
        -- validation error is never the way the person learns of it.

    @guidance
        -- The profile editor: display name, bio, website, and whether new
        -- followers need approval. The post editor: caption, sensitive,
        -- content warning while sensitive; attachments are neither added
        -- nor removed. The report form: one of nine reasons and an
        -- optional note; after it is sent the form is replaced by a
        -- confirmation and Done.
}

surface ExploreScreen {
    facing viewer: Viewer
    context explore: Explore

    exposes:
        explore.query
        explore.status
        explore.searched_for when explore.status != not_searching
        explore.range
        explore.posts_loaded

    provides:
        SearchSubmitted(viewer, explore, term) when explore.status != searching
        ClearPressed(viewer, explore) when explore.status != not_searching
        RangePicked(viewer, explore, range)
}

surface ProfileScreen {
    facing viewer: Viewer
    context profile: ProfileView

    exposes:
        profile.account_id
        profile.account
        profile.relationship
        profile.is_self
        profile.busy
        profile.block_armed

        RelationChange

    provides:
        RelationPressed(viewer, profile, change) when profile.relationship != null and not profile.is_self
        BlockPressed(viewer, profile) when profile.relationship != null and not profile.is_self
        BlockCancelled(viewer, profile) when profile.block_armed

    @guidance
        -- The header: avatar, the three counts (followers and following
        -- open their lists), names with a lock when locked, Follows you,
        -- the plain-text bio, the website as text. For another account:
        -- Follow and Message, then Mute, Block and Report; a blocked
        -- account shows Unblock in place of Follow and no Message. For the
        -- viewer's own: Edit profile, and Settings in the header. The grid
        -- is three tiles wide. The Me tab is this surface with the
        -- session's account id.
}

surface ThreadScreen {
    facing viewer: Viewer
    context thread: ThreadView

    exposes:
        thread.other_account_id
        thread.draft
        thread.sending
        thread.send_error

    provides:
        MessageSubmitted(viewer, thread, text) when not thread.sending
}

surface NotificationsScreen {
    facing viewer: Viewer

    provides:
        NotificationPressed(viewer, notification)

    @guidance
        -- A row reads "<actor> <phrase>" with the phrases pixelfed-rn
        -- uses; below it one line of the post concerned and to the right
        -- its first attachment's preview, blank when the post is
        -- sensitive. "Someone" stands in for a missing actor.
}

surface ComposeScreen {
    facing viewer: Viewer
    context composer: Composer

    exposes:
        composer.settings
        composer.caption
        composer.visibility
        composer.sensitive
        composer.spoiler_text
        composer.comments_disabled
        composer.status
        composer.post_error when composer.status = post_failed
        composer.can_post
        for item in composer.items:
            item.key
            item.name
            item.mime
            item.size_bytes
            item.status
            item.alt_text
            item.alt_saved
            item.alt_busy

    provides:
        FilePicked(viewer, composer, name, mime, size_bytes)
        PostPressed(viewer, composer) when composer.can_post
        CaptionEdited(viewer, composer, text)

    @guarantee NothingLeavesWithoutIntent
        -- Bytes leave the device only for a file the person picked, to
        -- the logged-in instance, once. Nothing is uploaded on behalf of
        -- a draft, a paste or a drop.
}

surface SettingsScreen {
    facing viewer: Viewer
    context settings: SettingsView

    exposes:
        settings.logout_armed

    provides:
        LogoutPressed(viewer, settings) when not settings.logout_armed
        StayPressed(viewer, settings) when settings.logout_armed
        LogoutConfirmed(viewer, settings) when settings.logout_armed

    @guidance
        -- Entries: Edit profile, Follow requests, Messages; Bookmarks,
        -- Likes, Followed hashtags; Muted accounts, Blocked accounts; the
        -- session line and Log out.
}

-- The repository as a developer meets it.
surface DevShell {
    facing developer: Core

    exposes:
        developer.session
        for issue in KnownIssues where status = open:
            issue.name
            issue.effect
            issue.closes_when

    @guarantee NoNodeModules
        -- The repository has no package.json; esbuild and node come from
        -- nixpkgs, esbuild driven by spago bundle and node by spago test.

    @guidance
        -- flake.nix devShells.default: purs, spago, purs-tidy,
        -- purs-backend-es, purescript-language-server, esbuild, nodejs,
        -- rust stable with rust-src and rust-analyzer, cargo-tauri,
        -- pkg-config, gobject-introspection, WebKitGTK 4.1 and GTK 3 and
        -- their libraries, glib-networking, xdg-utils, and GStreamer with
        -- gst-plugins-base, -good, -bad and gst-libav. The shell sets
        -- GST_PLUGIN_SYSTEM_PATH_1_0 to exactly those five, so the
        -- webview's media plugins are the flake's and match the GStreamer
        -- WebKitGTK is linked to (KnownIssue video_playback_unseen).
        -- Commands: nix develop; spago build, spago test, spago bundle;
        -- cargo tauri icon <png> once; cargo tauri dev; fish
        -- scripts/check.fish. The session file lands in
        -- ~/.local/share/com.harryprayiv.pellucid/. A server on the same
        -- machine: in the pellucid-server repository, fish
        -- scripts/dev.fish db-start, create-account NAME and serve, then
        -- sign in here to http://127.0.0.1:8080 (D34).
        -- devShells.android adds the Android SDK 34, NDK 26.1.10909125,
        -- JDK 17 and the four Android Rust targets (KnownIssue
        -- android_shell_untested).
}

-- The throwaway Pixelfed on blade (D16).
surface LabInstance {
    facing lab: Instance

    exposes:
        lab.domain

    @guarantee RealCertificate
        -- Let's Encrypt by DNS-01, so the client's https-only rule (D5)
        -- holds against the lab exactly as it does against
        -- pixelfed.social. The host is never reachable from outside; only
        -- the DNS record is public.

    @guarantee Disposable
        -- Removing the import and /var/lib/pixelfed (and the MySQL
        -- database the module created) leaves nothing behind.

    @guidance
        -- lab.pixelfed.{enable, domain, acme.{email, dnsProvider,
        -- environmentFile}, envSecretFile, openFirewall}: Pixelfed with
        -- open registration, no email verification, mail to the journal,
        -- every ActivityPub switch off, OAuth on. pixelfed-manage
        -- user:create --name --username --email --password --is_admin=1
        -- --confirm_email=1. KnownIssue lab_instance_undeployed.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Deferred Specifications
------------------------------------------------------------

deferred OAuth2.authorization_code     -- see: RFC 6749 section 4.1 and RFC 7636
deferred Mastodon.api                  -- see: https://docs.joinmastodon.org/methods/
deferred Pixelfed.api                  -- see: app/Http/Controllers/Api/ApiV1Controller.php and routes/api.php in pixelfed/pixelfed
deferred Pixelfed.entities             -- see: app/Transformer/Api/*.php and app/Services/StatusService.php
deferred Tauri.config                  -- see: https://schema.tauri.app/config/2
deferred Tauri.mobile                  -- see: cargo tauri android init, tauri-plugin-deep-link
deferred Nixpkgs.pixelfed              -- see: nixos/modules/services/web-apps/pixelfed.nix
deferred Pellucid.server               -- see: pellucid-server.allium in the pellucid-server repository

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open Questions
------------------------------------------------------------

open question "Whether an uploaded item removed from the composer should be deleted on the server at once (KnownIssue orphan_uploads). Pixelfed's API has no documented DELETE /api/v1/media/{id}."
open question "Which secret store the Android shell uses: Android Keystore through a small Kotlin plugin, or tauri-plugin-stronghold with a key derived on device. The trait fixes the interface either way."
open question "Whether the lab instance should federate at all. Off keeps it disposable and unreachable; on would let the client be tested against remote accounts and media proxying."
open question "Whether feeds should window their rendering once a session has scrolled through hundreds of posts. Screens now stay mounted (D24), so a long feed costs memory for as long as its tab is open; the point at which that matters is unmeasured."
open question "Whether the screens' own state machines (detail, profile, compose, thread, forms) should be pulled out of the Halogen components into pure modules the way App.Paged and App.Stack were, so that spago test covers them and the headless run is no longer the only thing that does."
open question "Whether a like or a share should show at once and roll back on failure. D9 waits for the server; on a slow connection the button reads as dead for the length of the request."
open question "Whether the name Pellucid collides with a mark in app stores or in the fediverse client space. A proper check is before D18, not after."
open question "Whether the Tauri shell needs the isolation pattern once the app renders content from many servers, or whether D6 plus the CSP is enough."
